    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-142bd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "142BD Designated carriage service",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-142bd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, designated carriage service means:\n\n(a) if a carriage service is specified in an instrument under\nsubsection (2)—that carriage service; or\n\n(b) otherwise—a Layer 2 bitstream service.\n\n(2) The ACCC may, by legislative instrument, specify a carriage\nservice for the purposes of paragraph (1)(a).\n\n(3) The ACCC must not specify a carriage service under subsection (2)\nunless:\n\n(a) the carriage service enables end-users to download\ncommunications; and\n\n(b) the download transmission speed of the carriage service is\nnormally 25 megabits per second or more; and\n\n(c) the carriage service is supplied using a line to premises\noccupied or used by an end-user; and\n\nLocal access lines  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(d) there is in force a declaration under subsection 152AL(3) of\nthe Competition and Consumer Act 2010 that relates to the\ncarriage service.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, designated carriage service means:\n\n(a) if a carriage service is specified in an instrument under\nsubsection (2)—that carriage service; or\n\n(b) otherwise—a Layer 2 bitstream service.\n\n(2) The ACCC may, by legislative instrument, specify a carriage\nservice for the purposes of paragraph (1)(a).\n\n(3) The ACCC must not specify a carriage service under subsection (2)\nunless:\n\n(a) the carriage service enables end-users to download\ncommunications; and\n\n(b) the download transmission speed of the carriage service is\nnormally 25 megabits per second or more; and\n\n(c) the carriage service is supplied using a line to premises\noccupied or used by an end-user; and\n\nLocal access lines  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(d) there is in force a declaration under subsection 152AL(3) of\nthe Competition and Consumer Act 2010 that relates to the\ncarriage service.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-142bd-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-142bd-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-142bd-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d279e7c2b35f7c527163c03881ce0143d0f257411cd8a2bc4a03fe2021419f20"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-142bd",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "142BD Designated carriage service",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, designated carriage service means:\n\n(a) if a carriage service is specified in an instrument under\nsubsection (2)—that carriage service; or\n\n(b) otherwise—a Layer 2 bitstream service.\n\n(2) The ACCC may, by legislative instrument, specify a carriage\nservice for the purposes of paragraph (1)(a).\n\n(3) The ACCC must not specify a carriage service under subsection (2)\nunless:\n\n(a) the carriage service enables end-users to download\ncommunications; and\n\n(b) the download transmission speed of the carriage service is\nnormally 25 megabits per second or more; and\n\n(c) the carriage service is supplied using a line to premises\noccupied or used by an end-user; and\n\nLocal access lines  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(d) there is in force a declaration under subsection 152AL(3) of\nthe Competition and Consumer Act 2010 that relates to the\ncarriage service."
    },
