    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-143c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "143C Judicial enforcement of conditions and limitations of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-143c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.34",
      "values:originalText": "exemption determinations\n\n(1) If the Federal Court is satisfied that a person has, on or after the\ndesignated commencement date, contravened any of the conditions\nor limitations of a determination under subsection 143A(1) or (2),\nthe Court may, on the application of:\n\n(a) the ACCC; or\n\n(b) a carrier; or\n\n(c) a carriage service provider;\nmake all or any of the following orders:\n\n(d) an order directing the person to comply with the condition or\nlimitation;\n\n(e) an order directing the person to compensate any other person\n(who may be the applicant) who has suffered loss or damage\nas a result of the contravention;\n\n(f) any other order that the Court thinks appropriate.\n\n(2) The Federal Court may discharge or vary an order granted under\nthis section.",
      "skos:definition": "exemption determinations\n\n(1) If the Federal Court is satisfied that a person has, on or after the\ndesignated commencement date, contravened any of the conditions\nor limitations of a determination under subsection 143A(1) or (2),\nthe Court may, on the application of:\n\n(a) the ACCC; or\n\n(b) a carrier; or\n\n(c) a carriage service provider;\nmake all or any of the following orders:\n\n(d) an order directing the person to comply with the condition or\nlimitation;\n\n(e) an order directing the person to compensate any other person\n(who may be the applicant) who has suffered loss or damage\nas a result of the contravention;\n\n(f) any other order that the Court thinks appropriate.\n\n(2) The Federal Court may discharge or vary an order granted under\nthis section.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-143c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-143c-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dc72f9d5526f3a8ec1d86b61f59fd4440abd4f7d904f2c13cf50c718fb7c76ae"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-143c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "143C Judicial enforcement of conditions and limitations of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 34,
      "values:originalText": "exemption determinations\n\n(1) If the Federal Court is satisfied that a person has, on or after the\ndesignated commencement date, contravened any of the conditions\nor limitations of a determination under subsection 143A(1) or (2),\nthe Court may, on the application of:\n\n(a) the ACCC; or\n\n(b) a carrier; or\n\n(c) a carriage service provider;\nmake all or any of the following orders:\n\n(d) an order directing the person to comply with the condition or\nlimitation;\n\n(e) an order directing the person to compensate any other person\n(who may be the applicant) who has suffered loss or damage\nas a result of the contravention;\n\n(f) any other order that the Court thinks appropriate.\n\n(2) The Federal Court may discharge or vary an order granted under\nthis section."
    },
