      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151b-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151B(3) Deemed standard functional separation undertaking",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151b-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.46",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If, as a result of an election under a determination under\nsubsection (1), a corporation is taken to have given a standard\nfunctional separation undertaking:\n\n(a) this Act does not prevent the corporation from giving the\nACCC another standard functional separation undertaking;\nand\n\n(b) if the other standard functional separation undertaking comes\ninto force—the corporation is taken to have cancelled the\nelection immediately before the other standard functional\nseparation undertaking comes into force.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If, as a result of an election under a determination under\nsubsection (1), a corporation is taken to have given a standard\nfunctional separation undertaking:\n\n(a) this Act does not prevent the corporation from giving the\nACCC another standard functional separation undertaking;\nand\n\n(b) if the other standard functional separation undertaking comes\ninto force—the corporation is taken to have cancelled the\nelection immediately before the other standard functional\nseparation undertaking comes into force.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151b-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151b-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4d4a0c20a839a3e8ab6f3047d2f078b25e2d0a7d28d2a5f858f52d3a4779a56f",
      "skos:note": "Corporation can give another standard functional separation undertaking without cancelling the previous one."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151b-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151B(3) Deemed standard functional separation undertaking",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 46,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If, as a result of an election under a determination under\nsubsection (1), a corporation is taken to have given a standard\nfunctional separation undertaking:\n\n(a) this Act does not prevent the corporation from giving the\nACCC another standard functional separation undertaking;\nand\n\n(b) if the other standard functional separation undertaking comes\ninto force—the corporation is taken to have cancelled the\nelection immediately before the other standard functional\nseparation undertaking comes into force."
    },
