    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151b-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151B(4) Deemed standard functional separation undertaking",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151b-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.46",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If, as a result of an election under a determination under\nsubsection (1), a corporation is taken to have given a standard\nfunctional separation undertaking:\n\nSchedule 2  Local access lines\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(a) this Act does not prevent the corporation, together with one\nor more other persons, from giving the ACCC a joint\nfunctional separation undertaking; and\n\n(b) if the joint functional separation undertaking comes into\nforce—the corporation is taken to have cancelled the election\nimmediately before the joint functional separation\nundertaking comes into force.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If, as a result of an election under a determination under\nsubsection (1), a corporation is taken to have given a standard\nfunctional separation undertaking:\n\nSchedule 2  Local access lines\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(a) this Act does not prevent the corporation, together with one\nor more other persons, from giving the ACCC a joint\nfunctional separation undertaking; and\n\n(b) if the joint functional separation undertaking comes into\nforce—the corporation is taken to have cancelled the election\nimmediately before the joint functional separation\nundertaking comes into force.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151b-ss-4-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b94707ba9c081ed242612455cac68a1e13f092e6de3c4ace44c951193f520a08",
      "skos:note": "Joint functional separation undertaking"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151b-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151B(4) Deemed standard functional separation undertaking",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 46,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If, as a result of an election under a determination under\nsubsection (1), a corporation is taken to have given a standard\nfunctional separation undertaking:\n\nSchedule 2  Local access lines\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(a) this Act does not prevent the corporation, together with one\nor more other persons, from giving the ACCC a joint\nfunctional separation undertaking; and\n\n(b) if the joint functional separation undertaking comes into\nforce—the corporation is taken to have cancelled the election\nimmediately before the joint functional separation\nundertaking comes into force."
    },
