    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151b-ss-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151B(7) Deemed standard functional separation undertaking",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151b-ss-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.46",
      "values:originalText": "(7) If:\n\n(a) a standard functional separation undertaking is in force as the\nresult of an election made by a person as mentioned in\nparagraph (1)(b); and\n\n(b) any of the following conditions is satisfied:\n\n(i) the person has breached a fundamental provision of the\nundertaking;\n\n(ii) the person has contravened section 151ZF or 151ZG;\n\n(iii) the ACCC is satisfied that the person has an\nunsatisfactory compliance record in relation to\nfunctional separation;\nthe ACCC may, by written notice given to the person, revoke the\nelection.",
      "skos:definition": "(7) If:\n\n(a) a standard functional separation undertaking is in force as the\nresult of an election made by a person as mentioned in\nparagraph (1)(b); and\n\n(b) any of the following conditions is satisfied:\n\n(i) the person has breached a fundamental provision of the\nundertaking;\n\n(ii) the person has contravened section 151ZF or 151ZG;\n\n(iii) the ACCC is satisfied that the person has an\nunsatisfactory compliance record in relation to\nfunctional separation;\nthe ACCC may, by written notice given to the person, revoke the\nelection.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151b-ss-7-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151b-ss-7-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151b-ss-7-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151b-ss-7-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151b-ss-7-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151b-ss-7-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3a78b015975719aff0617c1b99e1951ecd770a510f589e0fd1e3312795db37ae",
      "skos:note": "Revocation of standard functional separation undertaking election"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151b-ss-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151B(7) Deemed standard functional separation undertaking",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 46,
      "values:originalText": "(7) If:\n\n(a) a standard functional separation undertaking is in force as the\nresult of an election made by a person as mentioned in\nparagraph (1)(b); and\n\n(b) any of the following conditions is satisfied:\n\n(i) the person has breached a fundamental provision of the\nundertaking;\n\n(ii) the person has contravened section 151ZF or 151ZG;\n\n(iii) the ACCC is satisfied that the person has an\nunsatisfactory compliance record in relation to\nfunctional separation;\nthe ACCC may, by written notice given to the person, revoke the\nelection."
    },
