    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151f-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151F(5) ACCC to accept or reject functional separation undertaking",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151f-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.55",
      "values:originalText": "(5) The ACCC must take all reasonable steps to ensure that a decision\nabout the undertaking is made under subsection (2) within 3\nmonths after receiving the undertaking.\n\nSchedule 2  Local access lines\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020",
      "skos:definition": "(5) The ACCC must take all reasonable steps to ensure that a decision\nabout the undertaking is made under subsection (2) within 3\nmonths after receiving the undertaking.\n\nSchedule 2  Local access lines\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151f"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151f-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151f-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "df30779d301eaee46e12c55125573b6ba018f47c1bc70c524efb94ff71287b06",
      "skos:note": "ACCC must take steps to ensure a decision is made within 3 months after receiving the undertaking."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151f-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151F(5) ACCC to accept or reject functional separation undertaking",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 55,
      "values:originalText": "(5) The ACCC must take all reasonable steps to ensure that a decision\nabout the undertaking is made under subsection (2) within 3\nmonths after receiving the undertaking.\n\nSchedule 2  Local access lines\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151f-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151f-ss-5"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151f-ss-5-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to take steps within a timeframe.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151f-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151F(6) ACCC to accept or reject functional separation undertaking",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151f-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.55",
      "values:originalText": "(6) In calculating the 3-month period referred to in subsection (5),\ndisregard:\n\n(a) if:\n\n(i) the ACCC has given a notice under section 151K in\nrelation to the undertaking; and\n\n(ii) no varied undertaking was given to the ACCC in\nresponse to the notice;\n\na day in the period specified in the notice; and\n\n(b) if:\n\n(i) the ACCC has given a notice under section 151K in\nrelation to the undertaking; and\n\n(ii) a varied undertaking was given to the ACCC in\nresponse to the notice;\n\na day in the period:\n\n(iii) beginning on the day on which the notice was given;\nand\n\n(iv) ending at the end of the time limit specified by the\nACCC when it published the varied undertaking under\nsection 151G; and\n\n(c) if the ACCC has not given a notice under section 151K in\nrelation to the undertaking—a day in the period:\n\n(i) beginning on the day on which the ACCC published the\nundertaking under section 151G; and\n\n(ii) ending at the end of the time limit specified by the\nACCC when it published the undertaking under\nsection 151G; and\n\n(d) if the ACCC has requested further information under\nsection 151D in relation to the undertaking—a day during\nany part of which the request, or any part of the request,\nremains unfulfilled.\nExtension of decision-making period",
      "skos:definition": "(6) In calculating the 3-month period referred to in subsection (5),\ndisregard:\n\n(a) if:\n\n(i) the ACCC has given a notice under section 151K in\nrelation to the undertaking; and\n\n(ii) no varied undertaking was given to the ACCC in\nresponse to the notice;\n\na day in the period specified in the notice; and\n\n(b) if:\n\n(i) the ACCC has given a notice under section 151K in\nrelation to the undertaking; and\n\n(ii) a varied undertaking was given to the ACCC in\nresponse to the notice;\n\na day in the period:\n\n(iii) beginning on the day on which the notice was given;\nand\n\n(iv) ending at the end of the time limit specified by the\nACCC when it published the varied undertaking under\nsection 151G; and\n\n(c) if the ACCC has not given a notice under section 151K in\nrelation to the undertaking—a day in the period:\n\n(i) beginning on the day on which the ACCC published the\nundertaking under section 151G; and\n\n(ii) ending at the end of the time limit specified by the\nACCC when it published the undertaking under\nsection 151G; and\n\n(d) if the ACCC has requested further information under\nsection 151D in relation to the undertaking—a day during\nany part of which the request, or any part of the request,\nremains unfulfilled.\nExtension of decision-making period",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151f"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151f-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151f-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151f-ss-6-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151f-ss-6-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151f-ss-6-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151f-ss-6-logic-deontic-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151f-ss-6-logic-deontic-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ee01588f0f0a3da9ebab387d448ac8a861e850eaf909598ea457f2c8cb2ba3c7",
      "skos:note": "Disregard a day in the period specified in the notice when calculating the 3-month period."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151f-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151F(6) ACCC to accept or reject functional separation undertaking",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 55,
      "values:originalText": "(6) In calculating the 3-month period referred to in subsection (5),\ndisregard:\n\n(a) if:\n\n(i) the ACCC has given a notice under section 151K in\nrelation to the undertaking; and\n\n(ii) no varied undertaking was given to the ACCC in\nresponse to the notice;\n\na day in the period specified in the notice; and\n\n(b) if:\n\n(i) the ACCC has given a notice under section 151K in\nrelation to the undertaking; and\n\n(ii) a varied undertaking was given to the ACCC in\nresponse to the notice;\n\na day in the period:\n\n(iii) beginning on the day on which the notice was given;\nand\n\n(iv) ending at the end of the time limit specified by the\nACCC when it published the varied undertaking under\nsection 151G; and\n\n(c) if the ACCC has not given a notice under section 151K in\nrelation to the undertaking—a day in the period:\n\n(i) beginning on the day on which the ACCC published the\nundertaking under section 151G; and\n\n(ii) ending at the end of the time limit specified by the\nACCC when it published the undertaking under\nsection 151G; and\n\n(d) if the ACCC has requested further information under\nsection 151D in relation to the undertaking—a day during\nany part of which the request, or any part of the request,\nremains unfulfilled.\nExtension of decision-making period"
    },
    {
