    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151h",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151H Serial undertakings",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151h"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.57",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a person gives the ACCC a standard functional separation\nundertaking (the first functional separation undertaking);\nand\n\nSchedule 2  Local access lines\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(b) the ACCC rejects the first functional separation undertaking;\nand\n\n(c) the person subsequently gives the ACCC another standard\nfunctional separation undertaking; and\n\n(d) the ACCC is satisfied that any or all of the provisions of the\nfirst functional separation undertaking are materially similar\nto any or all of the provisions of the other functional\nseparation undertaking;\nthe ACCC may refuse to consider the other functional separation\nundertaking.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) 2 or more persons give the ACCC a joint functional\nseparation undertaking (the first functional separation\nundertaking); and\n\n(b) the ACCC rejects the first functional separation undertaking;\nand\n\n(c) those persons subsequently give the ACCC another joint\nfunctional separation undertaking; and\n\n(d) the ACCC is satisfied that any or all of the provisions of the\nfirst functional separation undertaking are materially similar\nto any or all of the provisions of the other functional\nseparation undertaking;\nthe ACCC may refuse to consider the other functional separation\nundertaking.\nRefund of fee\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) the ACCC refuses to consider a functional separation\nundertaking under this section; and\n\n(b) a person or persons have paid a fee in relation to the\nundertaking;\nthe ACCC must, on behalf of the Commonwealth, refund the fee.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a person gives the ACCC a standard functional separation\nundertaking (the first functional separation undertaking);\nand\n\nSchedule 2  Local access lines\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(b) the ACCC rejects the first functional separation undertaking;\nand\n\n(c) the person subsequently gives the ACCC another standard\nfunctional separation undertaking; and\n\n(d) the ACCC is satisfied that any or all of the provisions of the\nfirst functional separation undertaking are materially similar\nto any or all of the provisions of the other functional\nseparation undertaking;\nthe ACCC may refuse to consider the other functional separation\nundertaking.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) 2 or more persons give the ACCC a joint functional\nseparation undertaking (the first functional separation\nundertaking); and\n\n(b) the ACCC rejects the first functional separation undertaking;\nand\n\n(c) those persons subsequently give the ACCC another joint\nfunctional separation undertaking; and\n\n(d) the ACCC is satisfied that any or all of the provisions of the\nfirst functional separation undertaking are materially similar\nto any or all of the provisions of the other functional\nseparation undertaking;\nthe ACCC may refuse to consider the other functional separation\nundertaking.\nRefund of fee\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) the ACCC refuses to consider a functional separation\nundertaking under this section; and\n\n(b) a person or persons have paid a fee in relation to the\nundertaking;\nthe ACCC must, on behalf of the Commonwealth, refund the fee.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151h-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151h-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151h-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e2fecbb82901ae5f8b475b1488ad6ce19624f73e0b78a311cc91e2d6ba9ff37e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151h",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151H Serial undertakings",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 57,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a person gives the ACCC a standard functional separation\nundertaking (the first functional separation undertaking);\nand\n\nSchedule 2  Local access lines\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(b) the ACCC rejects the first functional separation undertaking;\nand\n\n(c) the person subsequently gives the ACCC another standard\nfunctional separation undertaking; and\n\n(d) the ACCC is satisfied that any or all of the provisions of the\nfirst functional separation undertaking are materially similar\nto any or all of the provisions of the other functional\nseparation undertaking;\nthe ACCC may refuse to consider the other functional separation\nundertaking.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) 2 or more persons give the ACCC a joint functional\nseparation undertaking (the first functional separation\nundertaking); and\n\n(b) the ACCC rejects the first functional separation undertaking;\nand\n\n(c) those persons subsequently give the ACCC another joint\nfunctional separation undertaking; and\n\n(d) the ACCC is satisfied that any or all of the provisions of the\nfirst functional separation undertaking are materially similar\nto any or all of the provisions of the other functional\nseparation undertaking;\nthe ACCC may refuse to consider the other functional separation\nundertaking.\nRefund of fee\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) the ACCC refuses to consider a functional separation\nundertaking under this section; and\n\n(b) a person or persons have paid a fee in relation to the\nundertaking;\nthe ACCC must, on behalf of the Commonwealth, refund the fee."
    },
