    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151l",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151L Replacement of functional separation undertaking that is",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151l"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.60",
      "values:originalText": "under consideration\nScope\n\n(1) This section applies if a person gives the ACCC a standard\nfunctional separation undertaking (the original undertaking).\nNotice\n\n(2) The ACCC may give the person a written notice stating that, if:\n\n(a) the person withdraws the original undertaking; and\n\n(b) the person, together with one or more other persons specified\nin the notice, gives a joint functional separation undertaking\nin the terms specified in the notice; and\n\n(c) the person does the things mentioned in paragraphs (a) and\n(b) within the time limit specified in the notice;\nthe ACCC would be inclined to accept the joint functional\nseparation undertaking.\n\n(3) The ACCC does not have a duty to consider whether to give a\nnotice under subsection (2).\n\nLocal access lines  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020",
      "skos:definition": "under consideration\nScope\n\n(1) This section applies if a person gives the ACCC a standard\nfunctional separation undertaking (the original undertaking).\nNotice\n\n(2) The ACCC may give the person a written notice stating that, if:\n\n(a) the person withdraws the original undertaking; and\n\n(b) the person, together with one or more other persons specified\nin the notice, gives a joint functional separation undertaking\nin the terms specified in the notice; and\n\n(c) the person does the things mentioned in paragraphs (a) and\n(b) within the time limit specified in the notice;\nthe ACCC would be inclined to accept the joint functional\nseparation undertaking.\n\n(3) The ACCC does not have a duty to consider whether to give a\nnotice under subsection (2).\n\nLocal access lines  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151l-ss-1"
        },
        {
