    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151q",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151Q Variation of functional separation undertaking that is in force",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151q"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.64",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a standard functional separation undertaking given by a\nperson is in force; or\n\n(b) a joint functional separation undertaking given by 2 or more\npersons is in force.\nVariation\n\n(2) The person or persons may give the ACCC a variation of the\nundertaking.\n\n(3) If the undertaking is a standard functional separation undertaking,\nthe undertaking as varied must comply with subsections 151A(2),\n(5), (8), (9), (10) and (11) and paragraph 151A(4)(a).\n\n(4) If the undertaking is a joint functional separation undertaking, the\nundertaking as varied must comply with subsections 151C(2), (5),\n(8), (9), (10), (11), (12) and (13) and paragraph 151C(4)(a).\nForm etc.\n\n(5) The variation must:\n\n(a) be accompanied by such information as is reasonably likely\nto assist the ACCC to decide whether to accept or reject the\nvariation; and\n\nLocal access lines  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(b) be accompanied by the fee (if any) specified in, or\nascertained in accordance with, a determination under\nsubsection (6).\n\n(6) The ACCC may, by legislative instrument, determine a fee, or a\nmethod of ascertaining a fee, for the purposes of paragraph (5)(b).\n\n(7) A fee determined under, or ascertained in accordance with,\nsubsection (6) must not be such as to amount to taxation.",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a standard functional separation undertaking given by a\nperson is in force; or\n\n(b) a joint functional separation undertaking given by 2 or more\npersons is in force.\nVariation\n\n(2) The person or persons may give the ACCC a variation of the\nundertaking.\n\n(3) If the undertaking is a standard functional separation undertaking,\nthe undertaking as varied must comply with subsections 151A(2),\n(5), (8), (9), (10) and (11) and paragraph 151A(4)(a).\n\n(4) If the undertaking is a joint functional separation undertaking, the\nundertaking as varied must comply with subsections 151C(2), (5),\n(8), (9), (10), (11), (12) and (13) and paragraph 151C(4)(a).\nForm etc.\n\n(5) The variation must:\n\n(a) be accompanied by such information as is reasonably likely\nto assist the ACCC to decide whether to accept or reject the\nvariation; and\n\nLocal access lines  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(b) be accompanied by the fee (if any) specified in, or\nascertained in accordance with, a determination under\nsubsection (6).\n\n(6) The ACCC may, by legislative instrument, determine a fee, or a\nmethod of ascertaining a fee, for the purposes of paragraph (5)(b).\n\n(7) A fee determined under, or ascertained in accordance with,\nsubsection (6) must not be such as to amount to taxation.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151q-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151q-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151q-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151q-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151q-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151q-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151q-ss-7"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151q",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151Q Variation of functional separation undertaking that is in force",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 64,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a standard functional separation undertaking given by a\nperson is in force; or\n\n(b) a joint functional separation undertaking given by 2 or more\npersons is in force.\nVariation\n\n(2) The person or persons may give the ACCC a variation of the\nundertaking.\n\n(3) If the undertaking is a standard functional separation undertaking,\nthe undertaking as varied must comply with subsections 151A(2),\n(5), (8), (9), (10) and (11) and paragraph 151A(4)(a).\n\n(4) If the undertaking is a joint functional separation undertaking, the\nundertaking as varied must comply with subsections 151C(2), (5),\n(8), (9), (10), (11), (12) and (13) and paragraph 151C(4)(a).\nForm etc.\n\n(5) The variation must:\n\n(a) be accompanied by such information as is reasonably likely\nto assist the ACCC to decide whether to accept or reject the\nvariation; and\n\nLocal access lines  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(b) be accompanied by the fee (if any) specified in, or\nascertained in accordance with, a determination under\nsubsection (6).\n\n(6) The ACCC may, by legislative instrument, determine a fee, or a\nmethod of ascertaining a fee, for the purposes of paragraph (5)(b).\n\n(7) A fee determined under, or ascertained in accordance with,\nsubsection (6) must not be such as to amount to taxation."
    },
