    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151s",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151S Withdrawal of variation that is under consideration",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151s"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.65",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a person gives the ACCC a variation of a standard functional\nseparation undertaking; or\n\n(b) 2 or more persons give the ACCC a variation of a joint\nfunctional separation undertaking.\n\nSchedule 2  Local access lines\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\nWithdrawal\n\n(2) The person or persons may withdraw the variation at any time\nbefore the ACCC makes a decision to accept or reject the variation.\n\n(3) This Act does not prevent the person or persons from giving a fresh\nvariation.\nRefund of fee\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) the person or persons withdraw the variation; and\n\n(b) the person or persons have paid a fee in relation to the\nvariation;\nthe ACCC may, on behalf of the Commonwealth, refund the whole\nor a part of the fee.",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a person gives the ACCC a variation of a standard functional\nseparation undertaking; or\n\n(b) 2 or more persons give the ACCC a variation of a joint\nfunctional separation undertaking.\n\nSchedule 2  Local access lines\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\nWithdrawal\n\n(2) The person or persons may withdraw the variation at any time\nbefore the ACCC makes a decision to accept or reject the variation.\n\n(3) This Act does not prevent the person or persons from giving a fresh\nvariation.\nRefund of fee\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) the person or persons withdraw the variation; and\n\n(b) the person or persons have paid a fee in relation to the\nvariation;\nthe ACCC may, on behalf of the Commonwealth, refund the whole\nor a part of the fee.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151s-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151s-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151s-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151s-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151s",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151S Withdrawal of variation that is under consideration",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 65,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a person gives the ACCC a variation of a standard functional\nseparation undertaking; or\n\n(b) 2 or more persons give the ACCC a variation of a joint\nfunctional separation undertaking.\n\nSchedule 2  Local access lines\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\nWithdrawal\n\n(2) The person or persons may withdraw the variation at any time\nbefore the ACCC makes a decision to accept or reject the variation.\n\n(3) This Act does not prevent the person or persons from giving a fresh\nvariation.\nRefund of fee\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) the person or persons withdraw the variation; and\n\n(b) the person or persons have paid a fee in relation to the\nvariation;\nthe ACCC may, on behalf of the Commonwealth, refund the whole\nor a part of the fee."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151s-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151S(1) Withdrawal of variation that is under consideration",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
