    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151t-ss-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151T(7) ACCC to accept or reject variation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151t-ss-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.66",
      "values:originalText": "(7) The ACCC may, by written notice given to the person or persons,\nextend the 3-month period referred to in subsection (5) (the initial\n3-month period), so long as:\n\n(a) the extension is for a period of not more than 3 months; and\n\n(b) the notice includes a statement explaining why the ACCC has\nbeen unable to make a decision on the variation within the\ninitial 3-month period.",
      "skos:definition": "(7) The ACCC may, by written notice given to the person or persons,\nextend the 3-month period referred to in subsection (5) (the initial\n3-month period), so long as:\n\n(a) the extension is for a period of not more than 3 months; and\n\n(b) the notice includes a statement explaining why the ACCC has\nbeen unable to make a decision on the variation within the\ninitial 3-month period.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151t"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151t-ss-7-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151t-ss-7-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151t-ss-7-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "89b9a2a52a68fc3da4e907c5e4d180dd49363e6c1785b85d0d19a221f10dcb40",
      "skos:note": "ACCC may extend initial 3-month period for decision on variation",
      "dc:description": "written notice with explanation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151t-ss-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151T(7) ACCC to accept or reject variation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 66,
      "values:originalText": "(7) The ACCC may, by written notice given to the person or persons,\nextend the 3-month period referred to in subsection (5) (the initial\n3-month period), so long as:\n\n(a) the extension is for a period of not more than 3 months; and\n\n(b) the notice includes a statement explaining why the ACCC has\nbeen unable to make a decision on the variation within the\ninitial 3-month period."
    },
