    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151u",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151U Consultation—acceptance or rejection of variation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151u"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.68",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a person gives the ACCC a variation of a standard functional\nseparation undertaking; or\n\n(b) 2 or more persons give the ACCC a variation of a joint\nfunctional separation undertaking.\nConsultation\n\n(2) Before making a decision to accept or reject the variation, the\nACCC must:\n\n(a) publish on the ACCC’s website a notice:\n\n(i) setting out the variation; and\n\n(ii) inviting persons to make submissions to the ACCC\nabout the variation within the time limit specified in the\nnotice; and\n\n(b) consider any submissions received within the time limit\nspecified in the notice.\n\n(3) The time limit must not be shorter than 15 business days after the\nnotice is published.",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a person gives the ACCC a variation of a standard functional\nseparation undertaking; or\n\n(b) 2 or more persons give the ACCC a variation of a joint\nfunctional separation undertaking.\nConsultation\n\n(2) Before making a decision to accept or reject the variation, the\nACCC must:\n\n(a) publish on the ACCC’s website a notice:\n\n(i) setting out the variation; and\n\n(ii) inviting persons to make submissions to the ACCC\nabout the variation within the time limit specified in the\nnotice; and\n\n(b) consider any submissions received within the time limit\nspecified in the notice.\n\n(3) The time limit must not be shorter than 15 business days after the\nnotice is published.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151u-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151u-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151u-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151u",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151U Consultation—acceptance or rejection of variation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 68,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a person gives the ACCC a variation of a standard functional\nseparation undertaking; or\n\n(b) 2 or more persons give the ACCC a variation of a joint\nfunctional separation undertaking.\nConsultation\n\n(2) Before making a decision to accept or reject the variation, the\nACCC must:\n\n(a) publish on the ACCC’s website a notice:\n\n(i) setting out the variation; and\n\n(ii) inviting persons to make submissions to the ACCC\nabout the variation within the time limit specified in the\nnotice; and\n\n(b) consider any submissions received within the time limit\nspecified in the notice.\n\n(3) The time limit must not be shorter than 15 business days after the\nnotice is published."
    },
    {
