    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151v",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151V Criteria for accepting variation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151v"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.68",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a person gives the ACCC a variation of a standard functional\nseparation undertaking; or\n\n(b) 2 or more persons give the ACCC a variation of a joint\nfunctional separation undertaking.\nCriteria\n\n(2) In deciding whether to accept the variation, the ACCC must have\nregard to:\n\nLocal access lines  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(a) whether the variation promotes the long-term interests of\nend-users of carriage services or of services supplied by\nmeans of carriage services; and\n\n(b) the matters (if any) specified in a determination under\nsubsection (3); and\n\n(c) such other matters (if any) as the ACCC considers relevant.\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine one or\nmore matters for the purposes of paragraph (2)(b).",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a person gives the ACCC a variation of a standard functional\nseparation undertaking; or\n\n(b) 2 or more persons give the ACCC a variation of a joint\nfunctional separation undertaking.\nCriteria\n\n(2) In deciding whether to accept the variation, the ACCC must have\nregard to:\n\nLocal access lines  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(a) whether the variation promotes the long-term interests of\nend-users of carriage services or of services supplied by\nmeans of carriage services; and\n\n(b) the matters (if any) specified in a determination under\nsubsection (3); and\n\n(c) such other matters (if any) as the ACCC considers relevant.\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine one or\nmore matters for the purposes of paragraph (2)(b).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151v-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151v-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151v-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151v",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151V Criteria for accepting variation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 68,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a person gives the ACCC a variation of a standard functional\nseparation undertaking; or\n\n(b) 2 or more persons give the ACCC a variation of a joint\nfunctional separation undertaking.\nCriteria\n\n(2) In deciding whether to accept the variation, the ACCC must have\nregard to:\n\nLocal access lines  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(a) whether the variation promotes the long-term interests of\nend-users of carriage services or of services supplied by\nmeans of carriage services; and\n\n(b) the matters (if any) specified in a determination under\nsubsection (3); and\n\n(c) such other matters (if any) as the ACCC considers relevant.\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine one or\nmore matters for the purposes of paragraph (2)(b)."
    },
