      "cml:integrityHash": "9fcdc9769b2897985d97cc15e03099ad04b11da91a22aa4738ba4422cccfe8b3",
      "skos:note": "ACCC must consider certain matters when deciding to accept a variation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151v-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151V(2) Criteria for accepting variation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 68,
      "values:originalText": "(2) In deciding whether to accept the variation, the ACCC must have\nregard to:\n\nLocal access lines  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(a) whether the variation promotes the long-term interests of\nend-users of carriage services or of services supplied by\nmeans of carriage services; and\n\n(b) the matters (if any) specified in a determination under\nsubsection (3); and\n\n(c) such other matters (if any) as the ACCC considers relevant."
    },
