      "cml:integrityHash": "38e0365578c3712302425d323970f411e714d9fd19e3647b0fb149057874edfb",
      "skos:note": "ACCC must give written notice and consider submissions before revoking joint functional separation undertaking."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151x-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151X(3) Consultation—revocation of functional separation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 72,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Before making a decision under subsection 151W(6) or (7) to\nrevoke a joint functional separation undertaking given by 2 or more\npersons, the ACCC must:\n\n(a) give each of those persons a written notice:\n\n(i) stating that the ACCC proposes to revoke the\nundertaking; and\n\n(ii) inviting those persons to make submissions to the\nACCC about the revocation within the time limit\nspecified in the notice; and\n\n(b) consider any submissions received within the time limit\nspecified in the notice."
    },
