    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151y",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151Y Notification that a person is at risk of having an unsatisfactory",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151y"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.73",
      "values:originalText": "compliance record in relation to functional separation\nScope\n\n(1) This section applies to:\n\n(a) a breach by a person of a functional separation undertaking\ngiven by the person, so long as the breach occurred when the\nundertaking was in force; and\n\n(b) a contravention by a person of section 143B, 151ZA, 151ZB,\n151ZF, 151ZG, 151ZH or 151ZI.\nNote:\nSee section 142B.\nNotification\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) a functional separation undertaking given by a person is in\nforce; and\n\n(b) the ACCC is aware of one or more breaches or\ncontraventions by the person; and\n\n(c) the ACCC is satisfied that those breaches or contraventions\ndo not mean that the person has an unsatisfactory compliance\nrecord in relation to functional separation; and\n\n(d) the ACCC is satisfied that, if there were to be a particular\nkind of additional breach or contravention by the person, the\nperson would have an unsatisfactory compliance record in\nrelation to functional separation;\nthe ACCC must:\n\n(e) give the person a written notice:\n\n(i) stating that the ACCC considers that the person is at risk\nof having an unsatisfactory compliance record in\nrelation to functional separation; and\n\n(ii) informing the person that an unsatisfactory compliance\nrecord is a ground for revoking the undertaking; and\n\n(f) do so as soon as practicable after becoming satisfied as\nmentioned in paragraph (d).\nNote:\nSee section 142B.\n\nSchedule 2  Local access lines\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(3) A failure to comply with subsection (2) does not affect the validity\nof a revocation of a functional separation undertaking.",
      "skos:definition": "compliance record in relation to functional separation\nScope\n\n(1) This section applies to:\n\n(a) a breach by a person of a functional separation undertaking\ngiven by the person, so long as the breach occurred when the\nundertaking was in force; and\n\n(b) a contravention by a person of section 143B, 151ZA, 151ZB,\n151ZF, 151ZG, 151ZH or 151ZI.\nNote:\nSee section 142B.\nNotification\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) a functional separation undertaking given by a person is in\nforce; and\n\n(b) the ACCC is aware of one or more breaches or\ncontraventions by the person; and\n\n(c) the ACCC is satisfied that those breaches or contraventions\ndo not mean that the person has an unsatisfactory compliance\nrecord in relation to functional separation; and\n\n(d) the ACCC is satisfied that, if there were to be a particular\nkind of additional breach or contravention by the person, the\nperson would have an unsatisfactory compliance record in\nrelation to functional separation;\nthe ACCC must:\n\n(e) give the person a written notice:\n\n(i) stating that the ACCC considers that the person is at risk\nof having an unsatisfactory compliance record in\nrelation to functional separation; and\n\n(ii) informing the person that an unsatisfactory compliance\nrecord is a ground for revoking the undertaking; and\n\n(f) do so as soon as practicable after becoming satisfied as\nmentioned in paragraph (d).\nNote:\nSee section 142B.\n\nSchedule 2  Local access lines\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(3) A failure to comply with subsection (2) does not affect the validity\nof a revocation of a functional separation undertaking.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151y-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151y-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151y-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "32ffcb005864d1a1ea0323748ad5963e259b06ad4f22eea3b71aa1844150842c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151y",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151Y Notification that a person is at risk of having an unsatisfactory",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 73,
      "values:originalText": "compliance record in relation to functional separation\nScope\n\n(1) This section applies to:\n\n(a) a breach by a person of a functional separation undertaking\ngiven by the person, so long as the breach occurred when the\nundertaking was in force; and\n\n(b) a contravention by a person of section 143B, 151ZA, 151ZB,\n151ZF, 151ZG, 151ZH or 151ZI.\nNote:\nSee section 142B.\nNotification\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) a functional separation undertaking given by a person is in\nforce; and\n\n(b) the ACCC is aware of one or more breaches or\ncontraventions by the person; and\n\n(c) the ACCC is satisfied that those breaches or contraventions\ndo not mean that the person has an unsatisfactory compliance\nrecord in relation to functional separation; and\n\n(d) the ACCC is satisfied that, if there were to be a particular\nkind of additional breach or contravention by the person, the\nperson would have an unsatisfactory compliance record in\nrelation to functional separation;\nthe ACCC must:\n\n(e) give the person a written notice:\n\n(i) stating that the ACCC considers that the person is at risk\nof having an unsatisfactory compliance record in\nrelation to functional separation; and\n\n(ii) informing the person that an unsatisfactory compliance\nrecord is a ground for revoking the undertaking; and\n\n(f) do so as soon as practicable after becoming satisfied as\nmentioned in paragraph (d).\nNote:\nSee section 142B.\n\nSchedule 2  Local access lines\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(3) A failure to comply with subsection (2) does not affect the validity\nof a revocation of a functional separation undertaking."
    },
