    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151z",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151Z Variation of functional separation undertaking following",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151z"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.74",
      "values:originalText": "giving of revocation notice\nStandard functional separation undertaking\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) the ACCC has given a notice under section 151W revoking a\nstandard functional separation undertaking; and\n\n(b) the revocation has not taken effect;\nthe ACCC may, by written notice given to the person who gave the\nundertaking, vary the undertaking.\n\n(2) The ACCC must not vary a standard functional separation\nundertaking under subsection (1) unless the variation:\n\n(a) addresses the matter or matters that constituted the grounds\nfor the revocation of the undertaking under section 151W;\nand\n\n(b) does not address any other matter.\nJoint functional separation undertaking\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) the ACCC has given a notice under section 151W revoking a\njoint functional separation undertaking; and\n\n(b) the revocation has not taken effect;\nthe ACCC may, by written notice given to each of the persons who\ngave the undertaking, vary the undertaking.\n\n(4) The ACCC must not vary a joint functional separation undertaking\nunder subsection (3) unless the variation:\n\n(a) addresses the matter or matters that constituted the grounds\nfor the revocation of the undertaking under section 151W;\nand\n\n(b) does not address any other matter.\n\nLocal access lines  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\nWhen variation takes effect\n\n(5) A variation under subsection (1) or (3) takes effect at the time the\nnotice is given.",
      "skos:definition": "giving of revocation notice\nStandard functional separation undertaking\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) the ACCC has given a notice under section 151W revoking a\nstandard functional separation undertaking; and\n\n(b) the revocation has not taken effect;\nthe ACCC may, by written notice given to the person who gave the\nundertaking, vary the undertaking.\n\n(2) The ACCC must not vary a standard functional separation\nundertaking under subsection (1) unless the variation:\n\n(a) addresses the matter or matters that constituted the grounds\nfor the revocation of the undertaking under section 151W;\nand\n\n(b) does not address any other matter.\nJoint functional separation undertaking\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) the ACCC has given a notice under section 151W revoking a\njoint functional separation undertaking; and\n\n(b) the revocation has not taken effect;\nthe ACCC may, by written notice given to each of the persons who\ngave the undertaking, vary the undertaking.\n\n(4) The ACCC must not vary a joint functional separation undertaking\nunder subsection (3) unless the variation:\n\n(a) addresses the matter or matters that constituted the grounds\nfor the revocation of the undertaking under section 151W;\nand\n\n(b) does not address any other matter.\n\nLocal access lines  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\nWhen variation takes effect\n\n(5) A variation under subsection (1) or (3) takes effect at the time the\nnotice is given.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151z-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151z-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151z-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151z-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151z-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "647f92746b00569c3aa7ea3a42b4b5ef66d44a91df45f493a792a3b03b2f5d6f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151z",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151Z Variation of functional separation undertaking following",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 74,
      "values:originalText": "giving of revocation notice\nStandard functional separation undertaking\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) the ACCC has given a notice under section 151W revoking a\nstandard functional separation undertaking; and\n\n(b) the revocation has not taken effect;\nthe ACCC may, by written notice given to the person who gave the\nundertaking, vary the undertaking.\n\n(2) The ACCC must not vary a standard functional separation\nundertaking under subsection (1) unless the variation:\n\n(a) addresses the matter or matters that constituted the grounds\nfor the revocation of the undertaking under section 151W;\nand\n\n(b) does not address any other matter.\nJoint functional separation undertaking\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) the ACCC has given a notice under section 151W revoking a\njoint functional separation undertaking; and\n\n(b) the revocation has not taken effect;\nthe ACCC may, by written notice given to each of the persons who\ngave the undertaking, vary the undertaking.\n\n(4) The ACCC must not vary a joint functional separation undertaking\nunder subsection (3) unless the variation:\n\n(a) addresses the matter or matters that constituted the grounds\nfor the revocation of the undertaking under section 151W;\nand\n\n(b) does not address any other matter.\n\nLocal access lines  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\nWhen variation takes effect\n\n(5) A variation under subsection (1) or (3) takes effect at the time the\nnotice is given."
    },
