    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151ZD Compliance with functional separation undertaking",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151zd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.78",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a functional separation undertaking given by a person is in force,\nthe person must comply with the undertaking.\n\nLocal access lines  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\nNote:\nSee also section 142B.\nAncillary contraventions\n\n(2) A person must not:\n\n(a) aid, abet, counsel or procure a contravention of\nsubsection (1); or\n\n(b) induce, whether by threats or promises or otherwise, a\ncontravention of subsection (1); or\n\n(c) be in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in,\nor party to, a contravention of subsection (1); or\n\n(d) conspire with others to effect a contravention of\nsubsection (1).\nCivil penalty provisions\n\n(3) Subsections (1) and (2) are civil penalty provisions.\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a functional separation undertaking given by a person is in force,\nthe person must comply with the undertaking.\n\nLocal access lines  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\nNote:\nSee also section 142B.\nAncillary contraventions\n\n(2) A person must not:\n\n(a) aid, abet, counsel or procure a contravention of\nsubsection (1); or\n\n(b) induce, whether by threats or promises or otherwise, a\ncontravention of subsection (1); or\n\n(c) be in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in,\nor party to, a contravention of subsection (1); or\n\n(d) conspire with others to effect a contravention of\nsubsection (1).\nCivil penalty provisions\n\n(3) Subsections (1) and (2) are civil penalty provisions.\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zd-ss-1"
        },
