    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zi",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151ZI Anti-avoidance",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151zi"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.88",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A corporation must not, either alone or together with one or more\nother persons:\n\n(a) enter into a scheme; or\n\n(b) begin to carry out a scheme; or\n\n(c) carry out a scheme;\nfor the sole or dominant purpose of avoiding the application of any\nprovision of this Part in relation to:\n\n(d) the corporation; or\n\n(e) any other corporation.\nAncillary contraventions\n\n(2) A person must not:\n\n(a) aid, abet, counsel or procure a contravention of\nsubsection (1); or\n\n(b) induce, whether by threats or promises or otherwise, a\ncontravention of subsection (1); or\n\n(c) be in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in,\nor party to, a contravention of subsection (1); or\n\n(d) conspire with others to effect a contravention of\nsubsection (1).\nCivil penalty provisions\n\n(3) Subsections (1) and (2) are civil penalty provisions.\n\nLocal access lines  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions.\nScheme\n\n(4) For the purposes of this section, scheme means:\n\n(a) any agreement, arrangement, understanding, promise or\nundertaking, whether express or implied; or\n\n(b) any scheme, plan, proposal, action, course of action or course\nof conduct, whether unilateral or otherwise;\nbut does not include a functional separation undertaking.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A corporation must not, either alone or together with one or more\nother persons:\n\n(a) enter into a scheme; or\n\n(b) begin to carry out a scheme; or\n\n(c) carry out a scheme;\nfor the sole or dominant purpose of avoiding the application of any\nprovision of this Part in relation to:\n\n(d) the corporation; or\n\n(e) any other corporation.\nAncillary contraventions\n\n(2) A person must not:\n\n(a) aid, abet, counsel or procure a contravention of\nsubsection (1); or\n\n(b) induce, whether by threats or promises or otherwise, a\ncontravention of subsection (1); or\n\n(c) be in any way, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in,\nor party to, a contravention of subsection (1); or\n\n(d) conspire with others to effect a contravention of\nsubsection (1).\nCivil penalty provisions\n\n(3) Subsections (1) and (2) are civil penalty provisions.\n\nLocal access lines  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions.\nScheme\n\n(4) For the purposes of this section, scheme means:\n\n(a) any agreement, arrangement, understanding, promise or\nundertaking, whether express or implied; or\n\n(b) any scheme, plan, proposal, action, course of action or course\nof conduct, whether unilateral or otherwise;\nbut does not include a functional separation undertaking.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zi-ss-1"
        },
