    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zl",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151ZL Review by the Australian Competition Tribunal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151zl"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.90",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the ACCC makes a decision under section 151F to reject a\nfunctional separation undertaking that was given by a person or\npersons, the person or persons may apply to the Australian\nCompetition Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(2) If the ACCC makes a decision under section 151N to vary a\nfunctional separation undertaking that was given by a person or\npersons, the person or persons may apply to the Australian\nCompetition Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(3) If the ACCC makes a decision under section 151T to reject a\nvariation that was given by a person or persons, the person or\npersons may apply to the Australian Competition Tribunal for a\nreview of the decision.\n\n(4) If the ACCC makes a decision under section 151W to revoke a\nfunctional separation undertaking that was given by a person or\npersons, the person or persons may apply to the Australian\nCompetition Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(5) If the ACCC makes a decision under section 151Z to vary a\nfunctional separation undertaking that was given by a person or\npersons, the person or persons may apply to the Australian\nCompetition Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(6) An application under this section for a review of a decision must\nbe:\n\n(a) in writing; and\n\n(b) in the case of an application under subsection (1), (3), (4) or\n(5)—made within 21 days after the ACCC made the decision;\nand\n\nLocal access lines  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(c) in the case of an application under subsection (2)—made\nwithin 14 days after the ACCC made the decision.\n\n(7) If the Australian Competition Tribunal receives an application\nunder this section for a review of a decision, the Australian\nCompetition Tribunal must review the decision.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the ACCC makes a decision under section 151F to reject a\nfunctional separation undertaking that was given by a person or\npersons, the person or persons may apply to the Australian\nCompetition Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(2) If the ACCC makes a decision under section 151N to vary a\nfunctional separation undertaking that was given by a person or\npersons, the person or persons may apply to the Australian\nCompetition Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(3) If the ACCC makes a decision under section 151T to reject a\nvariation that was given by a person or persons, the person or\npersons may apply to the Australian Competition Tribunal for a\nreview of the decision.\n\n(4) If the ACCC makes a decision under section 151W to revoke a\nfunctional separation undertaking that was given by a person or\npersons, the person or persons may apply to the Australian\nCompetition Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(5) If the ACCC makes a decision under section 151Z to vary a\nfunctional separation undertaking that was given by a person or\npersons, the person or persons may apply to the Australian\nCompetition Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(6) An application under this section for a review of a decision must\nbe:\n\n(a) in writing; and\n\n(b) in the case of an application under subsection (1), (3), (4) or\n(5)—made within 21 days after the ACCC made the decision;\nand\n\nLocal access lines  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(c) in the case of an application under subsection (2)—made\nwithin 14 days after the ACCC made the decision.\n\n(7) If the Australian Competition Tribunal receives an application\nunder this section for a review of a decision, the Australian\nCompetition Tribunal must review the decision.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zl-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zl-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zl-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zl-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zl-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zl-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zl-ss-7"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2b013cf310ddf628fc0390d24a6464ef84f6ecd103697314a509193a09738c83"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151zl",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151ZL Review by the Australian Competition Tribunal",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 90,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the ACCC makes a decision under section 151F to reject a\nfunctional separation undertaking that was given by a person or\npersons, the person or persons may apply to the Australian\nCompetition Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(2) If the ACCC makes a decision under section 151N to vary a\nfunctional separation undertaking that was given by a person or\npersons, the person or persons may apply to the Australian\nCompetition Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(3) If the ACCC makes a decision under section 151T to reject a\nvariation that was given by a person or persons, the person or\npersons may apply to the Australian Competition Tribunal for a\nreview of the decision.\n\n(4) If the ACCC makes a decision under section 151W to revoke a\nfunctional separation undertaking that was given by a person or\npersons, the person or persons may apply to the Australian\nCompetition Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(5) If the ACCC makes a decision under section 151Z to vary a\nfunctional separation undertaking that was given by a person or\npersons, the person or persons may apply to the Australian\nCompetition Tribunal for a review of the decision.\n\n(6) An application under this section for a review of a decision must\nbe:\n\n(a) in writing; and\n\n(b) in the case of an application under subsection (1), (3), (4) or\n(5)—made within 21 days after the ACCC made the decision;\nand\n\nLocal access lines  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(c) in the case of an application under subsection (2)—made\nwithin 14 days after the ACCC made the decision.\n\n(7) If the Australian Competition Tribunal receives an application\nunder this section for a review of a decision, the Australian\nCompetition Tribunal must review the decision."
    },
