    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151ZM(1) Functions and powers of the Australian Competition",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 91,
      "values:originalText": "(1) On a review of a decision of the ACCC of a kind mentioned in\nsection 151ZL, the Australian Competition Tribunal may make a\ndecision:\n\n(a) affirming the ACCC’s decision; or\n\n(b) setting aside the ACCC’s decision;\nand, for the purposes of the review, the Australian Competition\nTribunal may perform all the functions and exercise all the powers\nof the ACCC."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-1-norm",
