    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151ZM(3) Functions and powers of the Australian Competition",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.91",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If the Australian Competition Tribunal sets aside a decision of the\nACCC under section 151F to reject a functional separation\nundertaking, subsection 151F(5) has effect as if the undertaking\nhad been received by the ACCC immediately after the decision\nwas set aside.\nNote:\nThis subsection resets the start of the 3-month decision-making period\nset out in subsection 151F(5).",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If the Australian Competition Tribunal sets aside a decision of the\nACCC under section 151F to reject a functional separation\nundertaking, subsection 151F(5) has effect as if the undertaking\nhad been received by the ACCC immediately after the decision\nwas set aside.\nNote:\nThis subsection resets the start of the 3-month decision-making period\nset out in subsection 151F(5).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zm"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "90b1ef15db4675d8cfa6cbbeaf893fe3afce86df9323500977013a298f27f952",
      "skos:note": "Reset start of decision-making period after ACCC sets aside ACCC decision"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151ZM(3) Functions and powers of the Australian Competition",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 91,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If the Australian Competition Tribunal sets aside a decision of the\nACCC under section 151F to reject a functional separation\nundertaking, subsection 151F(5) has effect as if the undertaking\nhad been received by the ACCC immediately after the decision\nwas set aside.\nNote:\nThis subsection resets the start of the 3-month decision-making period\nset out in subsection 151F(5)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-3-norm",
