    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151ZM(4) Functions and powers of the Australian Competition",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.91",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If the Australian Competition Tribunal sets aside a decision of the\nACCC under section 151T to reject a variation, subsection 151T(5)\nhas effect as if the variation had been received by the ACCC\nimmediately after the decision was set aside.\nNote:\nThis subsection resets the start of the 3-month decision-making period\nset out in subsection 151T(5).\n\nSchedule 2  Local access lines\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\nConduct of review",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If the Australian Competition Tribunal sets aside a decision of the\nACCC under section 151T to reject a variation, subsection 151T(5)\nhas effect as if the variation had been received by the ACCC\nimmediately after the decision was set aside.\nNote:\nThis subsection resets the start of the 3-month decision-making period\nset out in subsection 151T(5).\n\nSchedule 2  Local access lines\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\nConduct of review",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zm"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-4-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-4-logic-ltl-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9fd4aa95269b60b588d2c79313367cd0f9507233e57ad9a56028f6b0b373bb8d",
      "skos:note": "Reset start of decision-making period after setting aside a decision"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151ZM(4) Functions and powers of the Australian Competition",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 91,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If the Australian Competition Tribunal sets aside a decision of the\nACCC under section 151T to reject a variation, subsection 151T(5)\nhas effect as if the variation had been received by the ACCC\nimmediately after the decision was set aside.\nNote:\nThis subsection resets the start of the 3-month decision-making period\nset out in subsection 151T(5).\n\nSchedule 2  Local access lines\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\nConduct of review"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Imposes an obligation on the ACCC to consider the variation immediately after a decision is set aside",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Australian Competition Tribunal sets aside a decision of the ACCC under section 151T",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Subsection 151T(5) has effect as if the variation had been received by the ACCC immediately after the decision was set aside"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-4-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Overlaps",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Describes a temporal relationship between the setting aside of a decision and the consideration of a variation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The variation is considered immediately after the decision is set aside",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The start of the 3-month decision-making period overlaps with the setting aside of a decision"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-4-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Recurrently",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Describes a recurring relationship between the setting aside of a decision and the consideration of a variation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The ACCC considers variations immediately after a decision is set aside",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The ACCC considers variations repeatedly over time"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151ZM(5) Functions and powers of the Australian Competition",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.91",
      "values:originalText": "(5) For the purposes of a review by the Australian Competition\nTribunal, the member of the Australian Competition Tribunal\npresiding at the review may require the ACCC to give such\ninformation, make such reports and provide such other assistance\nto the Australian Competition Tribunal as the member specifies.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) For the purposes of a review by the Australian Competition\nTribunal, the member of the Australian Competition Tribunal\npresiding at the review may require the ACCC to give such\ninformation, make such reports and provide such other assistance\nto the Australian Competition Tribunal as the member specifies.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zm"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e3e49b2ac2fe38687df42fe1950b32e0487743e0c1dbaa787b437f82a987c278",
      "skos:note": "The ACCC must provide information, reports, and assistance to the Australian Competition Tribunal."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151ZM(5) Functions and powers of the Australian Competition",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 91,
      "values:originalText": "(5) For the purposes of a review by the Australian Competition\nTribunal, the member of the Australian Competition Tribunal\npresiding at the review may require the ACCC to give such\ninformation, make such reports and provide such other assistance\nto the Australian Competition Tribunal as the member specifies."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-151zm-ss-5"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
