    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-162",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "162 Close proximity",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-2-sec-162"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.102",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if\nspecified circumstances exist in relation to premises and a line, the\npremises are taken, for the purposes of this Part, to be in close\nproximity to the line.\n\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if\nspecified circumstances exist in relation to premises and a line, the\npremises are taken, for the purposes of this Part, not to be in close\nproximity to the line.\n\n(3) A determination under subsection (1) or (2) must be of a legislative\ncharacter.\nDelegation to the ACCC\n\n(4) The Minister may, by writing, delegate to the ACCC any or all of\nthe Minister’s powers under the following provisions:\n\n(a) subsection (1);\n\n(b) subsection (2).\n\n(5) In performing a delegated function or exercising a delegated\npower, the ACCC must comply with any written directions of the\nMinister.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if\nspecified circumstances exist in relation to premises and a line, the\npremises are taken, for the purposes of this Part, to be in close\nproximity to the line.\n\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that, if\nspecified circumstances exist in relation to premises and a line, the\npremises are taken, for the purposes of this Part, not to be in close\nproximity to the line.\n\n(3) A determination under subsection (1) or (2) must be of a legislative\ncharacter.\nDelegation to the ACCC\n\n(4) The Minister may, by writing, delegate to the ACCC any or all of\nthe Minister’s powers under the following provisions:\n\n(a) subsection (1);\n\n(b) subsection (2).\n\n(5) In performing a delegated function or exercising a delegated\npower, the ACCC must comply with any written directions of the\nMinister.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-2-sec-162-ss-1"
        },
