      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.106",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n152BCCB  Statutory infrastructure provider standards and rules\nprevail over inconsistent access determinations\n\nAn access determination has no effect to the extent to which it is\ninconsistent with:\n\n(a) a standard determined under section 360U of the\nTelecommunications Act 1997; or\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(b) rules made under section 360V of that Act.",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n152BCCB  Statutory infrastructure provider standards and rules\nprevail over inconsistent access determinations\n\nAn access determination has no effect to the extent to which it is\ninconsistent with:\n\n(a) a standard determined under section 360U of the\nTelecommunications Act 1997; or\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(b) rules made under section 360V of that Act.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d0eb2b001171c998c38c87c62446b8ef7428cc7bc4b0f110244931ce4ea25470",
      "skos:note": "Inconsistent access determinations have no effect to the extent they contradict statutory infrastructure provider standards and rules."
    },
