    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360aa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360AA Qualifying fixed wireless carriage service",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-3-sec-360aa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.111",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, qualifying fixed wireless carriage\nservice means a carriage service, where:\n\n(a) the carriage service is supplied using a fixed wireless\ntechnology platform; and\n\n(b) the carriage service is marketed to customers, or potential\ncustomers, as a fixed wireless service; and\n\n(c) the carriage service enables end-users to download\ncommunications; and\n\n(d) the peak download transmission speed of the carriage service\nis at least 25 megabits per second; and\n\n(e) the peak upload transmission speed of the carriage service is\nat least 5 megabits per second; and\n\nSchedule 3  Statutory infrastructure providers etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, qualifying fixed wireless carriage\nservice means a carriage service, where:\n\n(a) the carriage service is supplied using a fixed wireless\ntechnology platform; and\n\n(b) the carriage service is marketed to customers, or potential\ncustomers, as a fixed wireless service; and\n\n(c) the carriage service enables end-users to download\ncommunications; and\n\n(d) the peak download transmission speed of the carriage service\nis at least 25 megabits per second; and\n\n(e) the peak upload transmission speed of the carriage service is\nat least 5 megabits per second; and\n\nSchedule 3  Statutory infrastructure providers etc.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360aa-norm"
        },
        {
