    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360B Simplified outline of this Division",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-3-sec-360b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.112",
      "values:originalText": "•\nThere are 4 types of service area, as follows:\n\n(a)\nan interim NBN service area;\n\n(b)\nthe general service area;\n\n(c)\na nominated service area;\n\n(d)\na designated service area.\n•\nInterim NBN service areas exist only before the designated\nday.\n•\nThe general service area exists only after the start of the\ndesignated day.\n•\nAn NBN corporation will be the statutory infrastructure\nprovider for an interim NBN service area.\n•\nNBN Co will be the statutory infrastructure provider for the\ngeneral service area.\n•\nA nominated service area is an area that is attributable to:\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(a)\na declaration made by a carrier; or\n\n(b)\ncertain carrier licence conditions declarations made by\nthe Minister.\n•\nThe statutory infrastructure provider for a nominated service\narea that is attributable to a declaration made by a carrier will\nbe:\n\n(a)\nthe carrier; or\n\n(b)\nanother carrier declared by the Minister.\n•\nThe statutory infrastructure provider for a nominated service\narea that is attributable to a carrier licence conditions\ndeclaration will be:\n\n(a)\nthe carrier to whom the carrier licence conditions\ndeclaration applies; or\n\n(b)\nanother carrier declared by the Minister.\n•\nA designated service area is an area declared by the Minister.\n•\nThe statutory infrastructure provider for a designated service\narea will be a carrier declared by the Minister.\n•\nNominated service areas and designated service areas are\nexcluded from interim NBN service areas and the general\nservice area.\n•\nDesignated service areas are excluded from nominated service\nareas.",
      "skos:definition": "•\nThere are 4 types of service area, as follows:\n\n(a)\nan interim NBN service area;\n\n(b)\nthe general service area;\n\n(c)\na nominated service area;\n\n(d)\na designated service area.\n•\nInterim NBN service areas exist only before the designated\nday.\n•\nThe general service area exists only after the start of the\ndesignated day.\n•\nAn NBN corporation will be the statutory infrastructure\nprovider for an interim NBN service area.\n•\nNBN Co will be the statutory infrastructure provider for the\ngeneral service area.\n•\nA nominated service area is an area that is attributable to:\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(a)\na declaration made by a carrier; or\n\n(b)\ncertain carrier licence conditions declarations made by\nthe Minister.\n•\nThe statutory infrastructure provider for a nominated service\narea that is attributable to a declaration made by a carrier will\nbe:\n\n(a)\nthe carrier; or\n\n(b)\nanother carrier declared by the Minister.\n•\nThe statutory infrastructure provider for a nominated service\narea that is attributable to a carrier licence conditions\ndeclaration will be:\n\n(a)\nthe carrier to whom the carrier licence conditions\ndeclaration applies; or\n\n(b)\nanother carrier declared by the Minister.\n•\nA designated service area is an area declared by the Minister.\n•\nThe statutory infrastructure provider for a designated service\narea will be a carrier declared by the Minister.\n•\nNominated service areas and designated service areas are\nexcluded from interim NBN service areas and the general\nservice area.\n•\nDesignated service areas are excluded from nominated service\nareas.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360b-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360b-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3fd3c72e24da97e0915ba9048abdd03731b37d12658bcb0896a6da6e8e821df0",
      "skos:note": "Defines types of service areas and their statutory infrastructure providers."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-3-sec-360b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "360B Simplified outline of this Division",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 112,
      "values:originalText": "•\nThere are 4 types of service area, as follows:\n\n(a)\nan interim NBN service area;\n\n(b)\nthe general service area;\n\n(c)\na nominated service area;\n\n(d)\na designated service area.\n•\nInterim NBN service areas exist only before the designated\nday.\n•\nThe general service area exists only after the start of the\ndesignated day.\n•\nAn NBN corporation will be the statutory infrastructure\nprovider for an interim NBN service area.\n•\nNBN Co will be the statutory infrastructure provider for the\ngeneral service area.\n•\nA nominated service area is an area that is attributable to:\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(a)\na declaration made by a carrier; or\n\n(b)\ncertain carrier licence conditions declarations made by\nthe Minister.\n•\nThe statutory infrastructure provider for a nominated service\narea that is attributable to a declaration made by a carrier will\nbe:\n\n(a)\nthe carrier; or\n\n(b)\nanother carrier declared by the Minister.\n•\nThe statutory infrastructure provider for a nominated service\narea that is attributable to a carrier licence conditions\ndeclaration will be:\n\n(a)\nthe carrier to whom the carrier licence conditions\ndeclaration applies; or\n\n(b)\nanother carrier declared by the Minister.\n•\nA designated service area is an area declared by the Minister.\n•\nThe statutory infrastructure provider for a designated service\narea will be a carrier declared by the Minister.\n•\nNominated service areas and designated service areas are\nexcluded from interim NBN service areas and the general\nservice area.\n•\nDesignated service areas are excluded from nominated service\nareas."
    },
