    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360g",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360G Statutory infrastructure provider for the general service area",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-3-sec-360g"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.116",
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of the application of this Part after the start of the\ndesignated day, NBN Co is the statutory infrastructure provider\nfor the general service area.\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\nSubdivision C—Rules applicable before, at and after the start\nof the designated day",
      "skos:definition": "For the purposes of the application of this Part after the start of the\ndesignated day, NBN Co is the statutory infrastructure provider\nfor the general service area.\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\nSubdivision C—Rules applicable before, at and after the start\nof the designated day",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360g-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a386b6f8279650733b8f6824f713e206c968640590d37cf5a1afbca30394a530",
      "skos:note": "Statutory infrastructure provider for the general service area"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-3-sec-360g",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "360G Statutory infrastructure provider for the general service area",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 116,
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of the application of this Part after the start of the\ndesignated day, NBN Co is the statutory infrastructure provider\nfor the general service area.\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\nSubdivision C—Rules applicable before, at and after the start\nof the designated day"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360g-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360g"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360h",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360H Nominated service area—declaration made by a carrier",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-3-sec-360h"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.117",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, if a provisional nominated service\narea is attributable to a declaration under this section, so much of\nthe provisional nominated service area as is not:\n\n(a) the whole or a part of a provisional nominated service area\nthat is attributable to a subsequent declaration under this\nsection; or\n\n(b) the whole or a part of a designated service area;\nis a nominated service area.\nProvisional nominated service area—real estate development\nproject\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) after the commencement of this section, a carrier (other than\nan NBN corporation) installs telecommunications network\ninfrastructure that will enable the supply of eligible services\nto premises in the whole of the project area of a real estate\ndevelopment project; and\n\n(b) the installation was carried out under a contract; and\n\n(c) the conditions specified in an instrument under subsection (3)\nare satisfied;\nthe carrier must:\n\n(d) by written instrument, declare that the whole of the project\narea is a provisional nominated service area for the purposes\nof this Part; and\n\n(e) do so within 10 business days after completing the\ninstallation of that infrastructure.\nNote:\nFor the format of the description of the area, see section 360LA.\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, specify conditions for\nthe purposes of paragraph (2)(c).\n\n(3A) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, exempt a specified\nreal estate development project from subsection (2).\n\nSchedule 3  Statutory infrastructure providers etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, if a provisional nominated service\narea is attributable to a declaration under this section, so much of\nthe provisional nominated service area as is not:\n\n(a) the whole or a part of a provisional nominated service area\nthat is attributable to a subsequent declaration under this\nsection; or\n\n(b) the whole or a part of a designated service area;\nis a nominated service area.\nProvisional nominated service area—real estate development\nproject\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) after the commencement of this section, a carrier (other than\nan NBN corporation) installs telecommunications network\ninfrastructure that will enable the supply of eligible services\nto premises in the whole of the project area of a real estate\ndevelopment project; and\n\n(b) the installation was carried out under a contract; and\n\n(c) the conditions specified in an instrument under subsection (3)\nare satisfied;\nthe carrier must:\n\n(d) by written instrument, declare that the whole of the project\narea is a provisional nominated service area for the purposes\nof this Part; and\n\n(e) do so within 10 business days after completing the\ninstallation of that infrastructure.\nNote:\nFor the format of the description of the area, see section 360LA.\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, specify conditions for\nthe purposes of paragraph (2)(c).\n\n(3A) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, exempt a specified\nreal estate development project from subsection (2).\n\nSchedule 3  Statutory infrastructure providers etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360h-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360h-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360h-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360h-ss-3a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9538b615b4d5f0dfb5ecb52bde450791099212d8c3f6a722257c26a7d055111d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-3-sec-360h",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "360H Nominated service area—declaration made by a carrier",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 117,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, if a provisional nominated service\narea is attributable to a declaration under this section, so much of\nthe provisional nominated service area as is not:\n\n(a) the whole or a part of a provisional nominated service area\nthat is attributable to a subsequent declaration under this\nsection; or\n\n(b) the whole or a part of a designated service area;\nis a nominated service area.\nProvisional nominated service area—real estate development\nproject\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) after the commencement of this section, a carrier (other than\nan NBN corporation) installs telecommunications network\ninfrastructure that will enable the supply of eligible services\nto premises in the whole of the project area of a real estate\ndevelopment project; and\n\n(b) the installation was carried out under a contract; and\n\n(c) the conditions specified in an instrument under subsection (3)\nare satisfied;\nthe carrier must:\n\n(d) by written instrument, declare that the whole of the project\narea is a provisional nominated service area for the purposes\nof this Part; and\n\n(e) do so within 10 business days after completing the\ninstallation of that infrastructure.\nNote:\nFor the format of the description of the area, see section 360LA.\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, specify conditions for\nthe purposes of paragraph (2)(c).\n\n(3A) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, exempt a specified\nreal estate development project from subsection (2).\n\nSchedule 3  Statutory infrastructure providers etc."
    },
