    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360p-ss-8",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360P(8) Obligation of statutory infrastructure provider to connect",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-3-sec-360p-ss-8"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.126",
      "values:originalText": "(8) If:\n\n(a) a carriage service provider makes a request as mentioned in\nsubsection (1) in relation to the connection of premises in a\nservice area; and\n\n(b) as a result, the statutory infrastructure provider has an\nobligation under subsection (1) to connect the premises; and\n\n(c) the statutory infrastructure provider has published on its\nwebsite:\n\n(i) the terms and conditions relating to price or a method of\nascertaining price; and\n\n(ii) other terms and conditions;\n\non which it offers to connect premises in the service area to a\nqualifying telecommunications network in order that a\ncarriage service provider can provide qualifying carriage\nservices to an end-user at the premises; and\n\n(d) the carriage service provider requests the statutory\ninfrastructure provider to enter into an agreement that:\n\n(i) relates to the connection of premises in the service area\nto a qualifying telecommunications network in order\nthat the carriage service provider can provide qualifying\ncarriage services to an end-user at the premises; and\n\n(ii) sets out terms and conditions that are the same as the\nterms and conditions published as mentioned in\nparagraph (c);\nthe statutory infrastructure provider must comply with the request\nmentioned in paragraph (d).\nNote:\nFor publication, see section 360W.",
      "skos:definition": "(8) If:\n\n(a) a carriage service provider makes a request as mentioned in\nsubsection (1) in relation to the connection of premises in a\nservice area; and\n\n(b) as a result, the statutory infrastructure provider has an\nobligation under subsection (1) to connect the premises; and\n\n(c) the statutory infrastructure provider has published on its\nwebsite:\n\n(i) the terms and conditions relating to price or a method of\nascertaining price; and\n\n(ii) other terms and conditions;\n\non which it offers to connect premises in the service area to a\nqualifying telecommunications network in order that a\ncarriage service provider can provide qualifying carriage\nservices to an end-user at the premises; and\n\n(d) the carriage service provider requests the statutory\ninfrastructure provider to enter into an agreement that:\n\n(i) relates to the connection of premises in the service area\nto a qualifying telecommunications network in order\nthat the carriage service provider can provide qualifying\ncarriage services to an end-user at the premises; and\n\n(ii) sets out terms and conditions that are the same as the\nterms and conditions published as mentioned in\nparagraph (c);\nthe statutory infrastructure provider must comply with the request\nmentioned in paragraph (d).\nNote:\nFor publication, see section 360W.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360p"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360p-ss-8-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360p-ss-8-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7e689c5bd53d0e95b487a55c4250478d8bb43a1f87857455bfc59523a11c0e49",
      "skos:note": "Statutory infrastructure provider must comply with request to connect premises."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-3-sec-360p-ss-8",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "360P(8) Obligation of statutory infrastructure provider to connect",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 126,
      "values:originalText": "(8) If:\n\n(a) a carriage service provider makes a request as mentioned in\nsubsection (1) in relation to the connection of premises in a\nservice area; and\n\n(b) as a result, the statutory infrastructure provider has an\nobligation under subsection (1) to connect the premises; and\n\n(c) the statutory infrastructure provider has published on its\nwebsite:\n\n(i) the terms and conditions relating to price or a method of\nascertaining price; and\n\n(ii) other terms and conditions;\n\non which it offers to connect premises in the service area to a\nqualifying telecommunications network in order that a\ncarriage service provider can provide qualifying carriage\nservices to an end-user at the premises; and\n\n(d) the carriage service provider requests the statutory\ninfrastructure provider to enter into an agreement that:\n\n(i) relates to the connection of premises in the service area\nto a qualifying telecommunications network in order\nthat the carriage service provider can provide qualifying\ncarriage services to an end-user at the premises; and\n\n(ii) sets out terms and conditions that are the same as the\nterms and conditions published as mentioned in\nparagraph (c);\nthe statutory infrastructure provider must comply with the request\nmentioned in paragraph (d).\nNote:\nFor publication, see section 360W."
    },
    {
