    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360r",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360R Notification obligations of statutory infrastructure provider",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-3-sec-360r"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.132",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if a carrier (the first carrier) is the statutory\ninfrastructure provider for:\n\n(a) a nominated service area; or\n\n(b) a designated service area.\nObligations\n\n(2) If the first carrier becomes aware that it is likely that it will no\nlonger be able to fulfil its obligations under section 360P or 360Q,\nso far as they relate to the area, the first carrier must:\n\n(a) give written notice of the matter to:\n\n(i) the Secretary of the Department; and\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(ii) the ACMA; and\n\n(b) do so as soon as practicable after becoming so aware.\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) subsection (2) applies; and\n\n(b) the first carrier becomes aware that another carrier is willing\nto become the statutory infrastructure provider for the area;\nthe first carrier must:\n\n(c) give written notice of the matter to:\n\n(i) the Secretary of the Department; and\n\n(ii) the ACMA; and\n\n(d) do so as soon as practicable after becoming so aware.",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if a carrier (the first carrier) is the statutory\ninfrastructure provider for:\n\n(a) a nominated service area; or\n\n(b) a designated service area.\nObligations\n\n(2) If the first carrier becomes aware that it is likely that it will no\nlonger be able to fulfil its obligations under section 360P or 360Q,\nso far as they relate to the area, the first carrier must:\n\n(a) give written notice of the matter to:\n\n(i) the Secretary of the Department; and\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(ii) the ACMA; and\n\n(b) do so as soon as practicable after becoming so aware.\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) subsection (2) applies; and\n\n(b) the first carrier becomes aware that another carrier is willing\nto become the statutory infrastructure provider for the area;\nthe first carrier must:\n\n(c) give written notice of the matter to:\n\n(i) the Secretary of the Department; and\n\n(ii) the ACMA; and\n\n(d) do so as soon as practicable after becoming so aware.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360r-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360r-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360r-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-3-sec-360r",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "360R Notification obligations of statutory infrastructure provider",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 132,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if a carrier (the first carrier) is the statutory\ninfrastructure provider for:\n\n(a) a nominated service area; or\n\n(b) a designated service area.\nObligations\n\n(2) If the first carrier becomes aware that it is likely that it will no\nlonger be able to fulfil its obligations under section 360P or 360Q,\nso far as they relate to the area, the first carrier must:\n\n(a) give written notice of the matter to:\n\n(i) the Secretary of the Department; and\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(ii) the ACMA; and\n\n(b) do so as soon as practicable after becoming so aware.\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) subsection (2) applies; and\n\n(b) the first carrier becomes aware that another carrier is willing\nto become the statutory infrastructure provider for the area;\nthe first carrier must:\n\n(c) give written notice of the matter to:\n\n(i) the Secretary of the Department; and\n\n(ii) the ACMA; and\n\n(d) do so as soon as practicable after becoming so aware."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360r-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360R(1) Notification obligations of statutory infrastructure provider",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-3-sec-360r-ss-1"
      },
