    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360r-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360R(3) Notification obligations of statutory infrastructure provider",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-3-sec-360r-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.132",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If:\n\n(a) subsection (2) applies; and\n\n(b) the first carrier becomes aware that another carrier is willing\nto become the statutory infrastructure provider for the area;\nthe first carrier must:\n\n(c) give written notice of the matter to:\n\n(i) the Secretary of the Department; and\n\n(ii) the ACMA; and\n\n(d) do so as soon as practicable after becoming so aware.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If:\n\n(a) subsection (2) applies; and\n\n(b) the first carrier becomes aware that another carrier is willing\nto become the statutory infrastructure provider for the area;\nthe first carrier must:\n\n(c) give written notice of the matter to:\n\n(i) the Secretary of the Department; and\n\n(ii) the ACMA; and\n\n(d) do so as soon as practicable after becoming so aware.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360r"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360r-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360r-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8e0985c81be6431db7b6750cdc8ceda634413ff59ab0de91c616362d853488fd",
      "skos:note": "First carrier must give written notice to Secretary and ACMA upon becoming aware of another carrier's willingness to become statutory infrastructure provider.",
      "dc:description": "written notice"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-3-sec-360r-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "360R(3) Notification obligations of statutory infrastructure provider",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 132,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If:\n\n(a) subsection (2) applies; and\n\n(b) the first carrier becomes aware that another carrier is willing\nto become the statutory infrastructure provider for the area;\nthe first carrier must:\n\n(c) give written notice of the matter to:\n\n(i) the Secretary of the Department; and\n\n(ii) the ACMA; and\n\n(d) do so as soon as practicable after becoming so aware."
    },
    {
