    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360s",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360S Targets for NBN Co",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-3-sec-360s"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.133",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Parliament intends that NBN Co should take all reasonable\nsteps to ensure that the telecommunications networks that:\n\n(a) are operated by NBN Co; and\n\n(b) are used to supply qualifying fixed-line carriage services to\ncustomers in Australia;\nare (when considered together) capable of being used to supply\nfixed-line carriage services, where:\n\n(c) the peak download transmission speed of the carriage service\nis at least 50 megabits per second; and\n\n(d) the peak upload transmission speed of the carriage service is\nat least 10 megabits per second;\nto at least 90% of premises in the areas that, according to NBN\nCo’s website, are serviced by NBN Co’s fixed-line carriage\nservices.\n\n(2) The Parliament intends that NBN Co should take all reasonable\nsteps to ensure that the telecommunications networks that:\n\n(a) are operated by NBN Co; and\n\n(b) are used to supply qualifying fixed-line carriage services to\ncustomers in Australia;\nare (when considered together) capable of being connected to at\nleast 92% of premises in Australia.\n\nSchedule 3  Statutory infrastructure providers etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Parliament intends that NBN Co should take all reasonable\nsteps to ensure that the telecommunications networks that:\n\n(a) are operated by NBN Co; and\n\n(b) are used to supply qualifying fixed-line carriage services to\ncustomers in Australia;\nare (when considered together) capable of being used to supply\nfixed-line carriage services, where:\n\n(c) the peak download transmission speed of the carriage service\nis at least 50 megabits per second; and\n\n(d) the peak upload transmission speed of the carriage service is\nat least 10 megabits per second;\nto at least 90% of premises in the areas that, according to NBN\nCo’s website, are serviced by NBN Co’s fixed-line carriage\nservices.\n\n(2) The Parliament intends that NBN Co should take all reasonable\nsteps to ensure that the telecommunications networks that:\n\n(a) are operated by NBN Co; and\n\n(b) are used to supply qualifying fixed-line carriage services to\ncustomers in Australia;\nare (when considered together) capable of being connected to at\nleast 92% of premises in Australia.\n\nSchedule 3  Statutory infrastructure providers etc.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360s-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360s-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "eedf18949001f76021d46a797d5e6a1fb92be5ef1c14aa8498678ee03ff38de1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-3-sec-360s",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "360S Targets for NBN Co",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 133,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Parliament intends that NBN Co should take all reasonable\nsteps to ensure that the telecommunications networks that:\n\n(a) are operated by NBN Co; and\n\n(b) are used to supply qualifying fixed-line carriage services to\ncustomers in Australia;\nare (when considered together) capable of being used to supply\nfixed-line carriage services, where:\n\n(c) the peak download transmission speed of the carriage service\nis at least 50 megabits per second; and\n\n(d) the peak upload transmission speed of the carriage service is\nat least 10 megabits per second;\nto at least 90% of premises in the areas that, according to NBN\nCo’s website, are serviced by NBN Co’s fixed-line carriage\nservices.\n\n(2) The Parliament intends that NBN Co should take all reasonable\nsteps to ensure that the telecommunications networks that:\n\n(a) are operated by NBN Co; and\n\n(b) are used to supply qualifying fixed-line carriage services to\ncustomers in Australia;\nare (when considered together) capable of being connected to at\nleast 92% of premises in Australia.\n\nSchedule 3  Statutory infrastructure providers etc."
    },
