    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360s-ss-1-logic-linearlogic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LinearLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "AND",
      "cml:logicSummary": "NBN Co's networks must meet both speed requirements and be used to supply qualifying fixed-line carriage services.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::linear",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) are operated by NBN Co;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...to at least 90% of premises in the areas that, according to NBN Co’s website, are serviced by NBN Co’s fixed-line carriage services."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360s-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360S(2) Targets for NBN Co",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-3-sec-360s-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.133",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Parliament intends that NBN Co should take all reasonable\nsteps to ensure that the telecommunications networks that:\n\n(a) are operated by NBN Co; and\n\n(b) are used to supply qualifying fixed-line carriage services to\ncustomers in Australia;\nare (when considered together) capable of being connected to at\nleast 92% of premises in Australia.\n\nSchedule 3  Statutory infrastructure providers etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The Parliament intends that NBN Co should take all reasonable\nsteps to ensure that the telecommunications networks that:\n\n(a) are operated by NBN Co; and\n\n(b) are used to supply qualifying fixed-line carriage services to\ncustomers in Australia;\nare (when considered together) capable of being connected to at\nleast 92% of premises in Australia.\n\nSchedule 3  Statutory infrastructure providers etc.",
