    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360u-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360U(5) Standards and benchmarks",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-3-sec-360u-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.134",
      "values:originalText": "(5) However, a statutory infrastructure provider is not required to\ncomply with a standard determined under subsection (1) to the\nextent that the standard is inconsistent with an access agreement to\nwhich the statutory infrastructure provider is a party, so long as:\n\n(a) the agreement was entered into before the commencement of\nthe standard; and\n\n(b) the agreement has not been varied after the commencement\nof the standard.\nPerformance benchmarks",
      "skos:definition": "(5) However, a statutory infrastructure provider is not required to\ncomply with a standard determined under subsection (1) to the\nextent that the standard is inconsistent with an access agreement to\nwhich the statutory infrastructure provider is a party, so long as:\n\n(a) the agreement was entered into before the commencement of\nthe standard; and\n\n(b) the agreement has not been varied after the commencement\nof the standard.\nPerformance benchmarks",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360u"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360u-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360u-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9431cb10183d339c2f8f6e23984e70a28cfca4a4d8ca9190a51339b6e8bd3fb6",
      "skos:note": "Exemptions from standards based on access agreements"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-3-sec-360u-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "360U(5) Standards and benchmarks",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 134,
      "values:originalText": "(5) However, a statutory infrastructure provider is not required to\ncomply with a standard determined under subsection (1) to the\nextent that the standard is inconsistent with an access agreement to\nwhich the statutory infrastructure provider is a party, so long as:\n\n(a) the agreement was entered into before the commencement of\nthe standard; and\n\n(b) the agreement has not been varied after the commencement\nof the standard.\nPerformance benchmarks"
    },
