        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360v-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2936d1a68c217eda982f702d5c6a984c28701fa45eb9142f1ffb44ba59befd97",
      "skos:note": "Exemption from rule compliance for access agreements entered before rule commencement"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-3-sec-360v-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "360V(3) Rules",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 136,
      "values:originalText": "(3) However, a statutory infrastructure provider is not required to\ncomply with a rule under subsection (1) to the extent that the rule\nis inconsistent with an access agreement to which the statutory\ninfrastructure provider is a party, so long as:\n\n(a) the agreement was entered into before the commencement of\nthe rule; and\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(b) the agreement has not been varied after the commencement\nof the rule."
    },
