    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360xa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "360XA Periodic compliance reports",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-3-sec-360xa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.138",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make rules requiring\neach statutory infrastructure provider to give to the ACMA\nperiodic reports relating to the provider’s compliance with this\nPart.\nCompliance\n\n(2) A statutory infrastructure provider must comply with rules under\nsubsection (1).\n\n(3) A person is not excused from giving a report under rules under\nsubsection (1) on the ground that the report might tend to\nincriminate the person or expose the person to a penalty.\n\n(4) However, in the case of an individual:\n\n(a) the report; or\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(b) giving the report; or\n\n(c) any information, document or thing obtained as a direct or\nindirect consequence of giving the report;\nis not admissible in evidence against the individual:\n\n(d) in civil proceedings for the recovery of a penalty; or\n\n(e) in criminal proceedings (other than proceedings for an\noffence against section 137.1 or 137.2 of the Criminal Code\nthat relates to the report).\nOther information-gathering powers not limited\n\n(5) This section does not, by implication, limit Part 27.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make rules requiring\neach statutory infrastructure provider to give to the ACMA\nperiodic reports relating to the provider’s compliance with this\nPart.\nCompliance\n\n(2) A statutory infrastructure provider must comply with rules under\nsubsection (1).\n\n(3) A person is not excused from giving a report under rules under\nsubsection (1) on the ground that the report might tend to\nincriminate the person or expose the person to a penalty.\n\n(4) However, in the case of an individual:\n\n(a) the report; or\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(b) giving the report; or\n\n(c) any information, document or thing obtained as a direct or\nindirect consequence of giving the report;\nis not admissible in evidence against the individual:\n\n(d) in civil proceedings for the recovery of a penalty; or\n\n(e) in criminal proceedings (other than proceedings for an\noffence against section 137.1 or 137.2 of the Criminal Code\nthat relates to the report).\nOther information-gathering powers not limited\n\n(5) This section does not, by implication, limit Part 27.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360xa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360xa-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360xa-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360xa-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-3-sec-360xa-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "595454217cf36dbbdeec767508997a70cee31c238e2877668ee9465176ca6bd0"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-3-sec-360xa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "360XA Periodic compliance reports",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 138,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make rules requiring\neach statutory infrastructure provider to give to the ACMA\nperiodic reports relating to the provider’s compliance with this\nPart.\nCompliance\n\n(2) A statutory infrastructure provider must comply with rules under\nsubsection (1).\n\n(3) A person is not excused from giving a report under rules under\nsubsection (1) on the ground that the report might tend to\nincriminate the person or expose the person to a penalty.\n\n(4) However, in the case of an individual:\n\n(a) the report; or\n\nStatutory infrastructure providers etc.  Schedule 3\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(b) giving the report; or\n\n(c) any information, document or thing obtained as a direct or\nindirect consequence of giving the report;\nis not admissible in evidence against the individual:\n\n(d) in civil proceedings for the recovery of a penalty; or\n\n(e) in criminal proceedings (other than proceedings for an\noffence against section 137.1 or 137.2 of the Criminal Code\nthat relates to the report).\nOther information-gathering powers not limited\n\n(5) This section does not, by implication, limit Part 27."
    },
