      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.145",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(4) The pecuniary penalty payable under subsection (1) by a person\nother than a body corporate is not to exceed:\n\n(a) in the case of a contravention of subsection 68(1) or (2) that\nrelates to the carrier licence condition set out in Part 1 of\nSchedule 1 in so far as that condition relates to\nsubsection 97(1) or (1A) of the Telecommunications\n(Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999—\n10,000 penalty units for each contravention; or\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(b) in any other case—$50,000 for each contravention.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(4) The pecuniary penalty payable under subsection (1) by a person\nother than a body corporate is not to exceed:\n\n(a) in the case of a contravention of subsection 68(1) or (2) that\nrelates to the carrier licence condition set out in Part 1 of\nSchedule 1 in so far as that condition relates to\nsubsection 97(1) or (1A) of the Telecommunications\n(Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999—\n10,000 penalty units for each contravention; or\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(b) in any other case—$50,000 for each contravention.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-6-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-6-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b7aa6b5fa5df211166b82d9abce301bf6f5bad6a3b41ae19ad38e1c0ad5a4aa7",
      "skos:note": "Maximum pecuniary penalty for contravention of subsection 68(1) or (2)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6 Subsection 570(4)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 145,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(4) The pecuniary penalty payable under subsection (1) by a person\nother than a body corporate is not to exceed:\n\n(a) in the case of a contravention of subsection 68(1) or (2) that\nrelates to the carrier licence condition set out in Part 1 of\nSchedule 1 in so far as that condition relates to\nsubsection 97(1) or (1A) of the Telecommunications\n(Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999—\n10,000 penalty units for each contravention; or\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(b) in any other case—$50,000 for each contravention."
    },
