      "cml:premiseText": "associate has the same meaning as in Part 8 of the Telecommunications Act 1997.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "associate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-76-logic-descriptionlogic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:DescriptionLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Class hierarchy",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "designated administrative costs means:\n\n(a) remuneration, and other employment-related costs and expenses, incurred in respect of APS employees whose duties relate to the performance of the ACMA’s functions, or the exercise of the ACMA’s powers, under this Part; or\n\n(b) any other costs, expenses and other obligations incurred by the ACMA in connection with the performance of the ACMA’s functions, or the exercise of the ACMA’s powers,\nunder this Part; or\n\n(c) remuneration, and other employment-related costs and expenses, incurred in respect of APS employees whose duties relate to the performance of the ACCC’s functions, or the exercise of the ACCC’s powers, under this Part or the Telecommunications (Regional Broadband Scheme) Charge Act 2020; or\n\n(d) any other costs, expenses and other obligations incurred by the ACCC in connection with the performance of the ACCC’s functions, or the exercise of the ACCC’s powers,\nunder this Part or the Telecommunications (Regional Broadband Scheme) Charge Act 2020;\nbut does not include:\n\n(e) amounts incurred under contracts made under section 80; and\n\n(f) amounts incurred by way of grants made under section 80.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "designated administrative costs"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-76a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "76A Local access line",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-76a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.152",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, a local access line is a line that is part\nof the infrastructure of a local access network.\n\n(2) However, a line does not form part of a local access line to the\nextent that the line is on the customer side of the boundary of a\ntelecommunications network.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) has effect subject to subsection (4).\n\n(4) For the purposes of this Part, if a line in a multi-unit building is\nused to supply a carriage service to a unit in the building, the line is\ntaken to be a local access line.\n\n(5) For the purposes of this section, the boundary of a\ntelecommunications network is to be determined in the same\nmanner in which it is determined under section 22 for the purposes\nof sections 20, 21 and 30.\n\n(6) For the purposes of this section, local access network has the\nmeaning generally accepted within the telecommunications\nindustry.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, a local access line is a line that is part\nof the infrastructure of a local access network.\n\n(2) However, a line does not form part of a local access line to the\nextent that the line is on the customer side of the boundary of a\ntelecommunications network.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) has effect subject to subsection (4).\n\n(4) For the purposes of this Part, if a line in a multi-unit building is\nused to supply a carriage service to a unit in the building, the line is\ntaken to be a local access line.\n\n(5) For the purposes of this section, the boundary of a\ntelecommunications network is to be determined in the same\nmanner in which it is determined under section 22 for the purposes\nof sections 20, 21 and 30.\n\n(6) For the purposes of this section, local access network has the\nmeaning generally accepted within the telecommunications\nindustry.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-76a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-76a-ss-2"
        },
