    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-76aa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "76AA Designated broadband services",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-76aa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.152",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, designated broadband service means\na carriage service that is supplied using a local access line, where:\n\n(a) the carriage service enables end-users to download\ncommunications; and\n\n(b) the local access line is part of the infrastructure of a\ntelecommunications network in Australia; and\n\nFunding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Schedule 4\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(c) the local access line is technically capable of being used to\nsupply a superfast carriage service;\nbut does not include:\n\n(d) a carriage service that can only be used by an end-user to\nmake and receive voice calls; or\n\n(e) a carriage service that can only be used by an end-user to\nview one or more broadcast television streams; or\n\n(f) a carriage service that belongs to a class determined under\nsubsection (2).\nNote:\nSee also section 102ZH.\n\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine one or\nmore classes of carriage service for the purposes of\nparagraph (1)(f).\nNote:\nSee also section 102ZFB (disallowance of determinations).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, designated broadband service means\na carriage service that is supplied using a local access line, where:\n\n(a) the carriage service enables end-users to download\ncommunications; and\n\n(b) the local access line is part of the infrastructure of a\ntelecommunications network in Australia; and\n\nFunding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Schedule 4\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(c) the local access line is technically capable of being used to\nsupply a superfast carriage service;\nbut does not include:\n\n(d) a carriage service that can only be used by an end-user to\nmake and receive voice calls; or\n\n(e) a carriage service that can only be used by an end-user to\nview one or more broadcast television streams; or\n\n(f) a carriage service that belongs to a class determined under\nsubsection (2).\nNote:\nSee also section 102ZH.\n\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine one or\nmore classes of carriage service for the purposes of\nparagraph (1)(f).\nNote:\nSee also section 102ZFB (disallowance of determinations).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-76aa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-76aa-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9dc443599a9ef6fd6922a78a609af239184c77c4b32f0fe0986b8eeadbc5be3e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-76aa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "76AA Designated broadband services",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 152,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, designated broadband service means\na carriage service that is supplied using a local access line, where:\n\n(a) the carriage service enables end-users to download\ncommunications; and\n\n(b) the local access line is part of the infrastructure of a\ntelecommunications network in Australia; and\n\nFunding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Schedule 4\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(c) the local access line is technically capable of being used to\nsupply a superfast carriage service;\nbut does not include:\n\n(d) a carriage service that can only be used by an end-user to\nmake and receive voice calls; or\n\n(e) a carriage service that can only be used by an end-user to\nview one or more broadcast television streams; or\n\n(f) a carriage service that belongs to a class determined under\nsubsection (2).\nNote:\nSee also section 102ZH.\n\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine one or\nmore classes of carriage service for the purposes of\nparagraph (1)(f).\nNote:\nSee also section 102ZFB (disallowance of determinations)."
    },
