    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-85",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "85 Monitoring of performance",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-85"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.159",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary must monitor, and report each financial year to the\nMinister on, all significant matters relating to:\n\n(a) the performance of contractors; and\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(b) the performance of grant recipients.\n\n(2) A report under subsection (1) for a financial year must set out\ndetails of the following matters:\n\n(a) the adequacy of each contractor’s compliance, during that\nyear, with the terms and conditions of a section 80 contract;\n\n(b) the adequacy of each grant recipient’s compliance, during\nthat year, with the terms and conditions of a section 80 grant;\n\n(c) any notice of breach by a contractor of a section 80 contract,\nwhere the notice was given during that year;\n\n(d) any notice of breach by a grant recipient of a term or\ncondition of a section 80 grant, where the notice was given\nduring that year;\n\n(e) any remedial action taken by the Secretary during that year in\nresponse to a breach of a section 80 contract;\n\n(f) any remedial action taken by the Secretary during that year in\nresponse to a breach of the terms or conditions of a\nsection 80 grant;\n\n(g) the result of any such remedial action.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit subsection (1).\n\n(4) A report under subsection (1) for a financial year must be included\nin the annual report prepared by the Secretary and given to the\nMinister under section 46 of the Public Governance, Performance\nand Accountability Act 2013 for the financial year.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretary must monitor, and report each financial year to the\nMinister on, all significant matters relating to:\n\n(a) the performance of contractors; and\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(b) the performance of grant recipients.\n\n(2) A report under subsection (1) for a financial year must set out\ndetails of the following matters:\n\n(a) the adequacy of each contractor’s compliance, during that\nyear, with the terms and conditions of a section 80 contract;\n\n(b) the adequacy of each grant recipient’s compliance, during\nthat year, with the terms and conditions of a section 80 grant;\n\n(c) any notice of breach by a contractor of a section 80 contract,\nwhere the notice was given during that year;\n\n(d) any notice of breach by a grant recipient of a term or\ncondition of a section 80 grant, where the notice was given\nduring that year;\n\n(e) any remedial action taken by the Secretary during that year in\nresponse to a breach of a section 80 contract;\n\n(f) any remedial action taken by the Secretary during that year in\nresponse to a breach of the terms or conditions of a\nsection 80 grant;\n\n(g) the result of any such remedial action.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit subsection (1).\n\n(4) A report under subsection (1) for a financial year must be included\nin the annual report prepared by the Secretary and given to the\nMinister under section 46 of the Public Governance, Performance\nand Accountability Act 2013 for the financial year.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-85-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-85-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-85-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-85-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3ae64a97ebba84f6bc643c0af5627838504f599d596bff6e7be790612cfcd7ef"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-85",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "85 Monitoring of performance",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 159,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary must monitor, and report each financial year to the\nMinister on, all significant matters relating to:\n\n(a) the performance of contractors; and\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(b) the performance of grant recipients.\n\n(2) A report under subsection (1) for a financial year must set out\ndetails of the following matters:\n\n(a) the adequacy of each contractor’s compliance, during that\nyear, with the terms and conditions of a section 80 contract;\n\n(b) the adequacy of each grant recipient’s compliance, during\nthat year, with the terms and conditions of a section 80 grant;\n\n(c) any notice of breach by a contractor of a section 80 contract,\nwhere the notice was given during that year;\n\n(d) any notice of breach by a grant recipient of a term or\ncondition of a section 80 grant, where the notice was given\nduring that year;\n\n(e) any remedial action taken by the Secretary during that year in\nresponse to a breach of a section 80 contract;\n\n(f) any remedial action taken by the Secretary during that year in\nresponse to a breach of the terms or conditions of a\nsection 80 grant;\n\n(g) the result of any such remedial action.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit subsection (1).\n\n(4) A report under subsection (1) for a financial year must be included\nin the annual report prepared by the Secretary and given to the\nMinister under section 46 of the Public Governance, Performance\nand Accountability Act 2013 for the financial year."
    },
