      "cml:conclusionText": "A person is not required to provide funding for fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband if they do not supply a designated service to potentially chargeable premises."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-95",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "95 Exempt premises—small networks",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-95"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.167",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a person is a member of an associated group during the whole\nor a part of a month; and\n\n(b) the total number of potentially chargeable premises in\nrelation to the members of the group for that month is less\nthan 2,000; and\n\n(c) one or more of those potentially chargeable premises are\npotentially chargeable premises in relation to the person for\nthat month;\neach of the potentially chargeable premises mentioned in\nparagraph (c) are exempt premises in relation to the person for that\nmonth.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) a person is not a member of an associated group during the\nwhole or a part of a month; and\n\n(b) the total number of potentially chargeable premises in\nrelation to the person for that month is less than 2,000;\neach of those potentially chargeable premises are exempt premises\nin relation to the person for that month.\nAssociated group\n\n(3) For the purposes of this section, if:\n\n(a) a person is in a position to exercise control of:\n\n(i) a local access line; or\n\n(ii) a telecommunications network; and\n\n(b) the person has one or more associates;\nthen:\n\n(c) the person is taken to belong to an associated group; and\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(d) the associated group consists of the person and those\nassociates.\n\n(4) For the purposes of subsection (3), the question of whether a\nperson is in a position to exercise control of:\n\n(a) a local access line; or\n\n(b) a telecommunications network;\nis to be determined in the same manner in which that question is\ndetermined for the purposes of Part 8 of the Telecommunications\nAct 1997.\n\n(5) For the purposes of subsection (3), the question of whether a\nperson has one or more associates is to be determined in the same\nmanner in which that question is determined for the purposes of\nPart 8 of the Telecommunications Act 1997.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a person is a member of an associated group during the whole\nor a part of a month; and\n\n(b) the total number of potentially chargeable premises in\nrelation to the members of the group for that month is less\nthan 2,000; and\n\n(c) one or more of those potentially chargeable premises are\npotentially chargeable premises in relation to the person for\nthat month;\neach of the potentially chargeable premises mentioned in\nparagraph (c) are exempt premises in relation to the person for that\nmonth.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) a person is not a member of an associated group during the\nwhole or a part of a month; and\n\n(b) the total number of potentially chargeable premises in\nrelation to the person for that month is less than 2,000;\neach of those potentially chargeable premises are exempt premises\nin relation to the person for that month.\nAssociated group\n\n(3) For the purposes of this section, if:\n\n(a) a person is in a position to exercise control of:\n\n(i) a local access line; or\n\n(ii) a telecommunications network; and\n\n(b) the person has one or more associates;\nthen:\n\n(c) the person is taken to belong to an associated group; and\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(d) the associated group consists of the person and those\nassociates.\n\n(4) For the purposes of subsection (3), the question of whether a\nperson is in a position to exercise control of:\n\n(a) a local access line; or\n\n(b) a telecommunications network;\nis to be determined in the same manner in which that question is\ndetermined for the purposes of Part 8 of the Telecommunications\nAct 1997.\n\n(5) For the purposes of subsection (3), the question of whether a\nperson has one or more associates is to be determined in the same\nmanner in which that question is determined for the purposes of\nPart 8 of the Telecommunications Act 1997.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-95-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-95-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-95-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-95-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-95-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3f1f53eec77f90ca2bd08afaa4ce72ed21789390712b46ba2731d2e75a7a6a28"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-95",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "95 Exempt premises—small networks",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 167,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a person is a member of an associated group during the whole\nor a part of a month; and\n\n(b) the total number of potentially chargeable premises in\nrelation to the members of the group for that month is less\nthan 2,000; and\n\n(c) one or more of those potentially chargeable premises are\npotentially chargeable premises in relation to the person for\nthat month;\neach of the potentially chargeable premises mentioned in\nparagraph (c) are exempt premises in relation to the person for that\nmonth.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) a person is not a member of an associated group during the\nwhole or a part of a month; and\n\n(b) the total number of potentially chargeable premises in\nrelation to the person for that month is less than 2,000;\neach of those potentially chargeable premises are exempt premises\nin relation to the person for that month.\nAssociated group\n\n(3) For the purposes of this section, if:\n\n(a) a person is in a position to exercise control of:\n\n(i) a local access line; or\n\n(ii) a telecommunications network; and\n\n(b) the person has one or more associates;\nthen:\n\n(c) the person is taken to belong to an associated group; and\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(d) the associated group consists of the person and those\nassociates.\n\n(4) For the purposes of subsection (3), the question of whether a\nperson is in a position to exercise control of:\n\n(a) a local access line; or\n\n(b) a telecommunications network;\nis to be determined in the same manner in which that question is\ndetermined for the purposes of Part 8 of the Telecommunications\nAct 1997.\n\n(5) For the purposes of subsection (3), the question of whether a\nperson has one or more associates is to be determined in the same\nmanner in which that question is determined for the purposes of\nPart 8 of the Telecommunications Act 1997."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-95-ss-1",
