        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-96b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "96B Recently connected greenfield premises",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-96b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.171",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) during a period comprising the whole or a part of a month in\nan eligible financial year, a person is a carrier; and\n\n(b) a declaration made under subsection 63(2) of the\nTelecommunications Act 1997 was in force on 30 June 2018\nin relation to the carrier licence held by the person; and\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(c) the declaration provides that the person must (upon request\nby an end-user at relevant premises) connect, or arrange for\nanother person on the person’s behalf to connect, premises\nlocated in a development area (however described) specified\nin the declaration to a telecommunications network owned by\nthe person (as specified in the declaration); and\n\n(d) the person, or another person on the person’s behalf:\n\n(i) has connected one or more premises located in the\ndevelopment area to the telecommunications network;\nand\n\n(ii) has done so before the end of 30 June 2019; and\n\n(e) one or more of the connected premises are potentially\nchargeable premises in relation to the person for that month;\neach of the potentially chargeable premises mentioned in\nparagraph (e) are recently connected greenfield premises in\nrelation to the person for that month.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) a person is a carrier; and\n\n(b) during a period comprising the whole or a part of a month in\nan eligible financial year, the person supplies an eligible local\nbitstream access service using a local access line; and\n\n(c) during a whole or a part of that period, a carriage service\nprovider supplies a designated broadband service to one or\nmore premises using the line; and\n\n(d) one or more of those premises are potentially chargeable\npremises in relation to the person for that month;\neach of the potentially chargeable premises mentioned in\nparagraph (d) are recently connected greenfield premises in\nrelation to the person for that month.\n\n(3) In this section:\neligible local bitstream access service means a local bitstream\naccess service that is first supplied at a time during the period:\n\n(a) beginning at the start of 1 January 2011; and\n\n(b) ending at the end of 30 June 2019.\nlocal bitstream access service has the meaning given by a\ndeclaration that:\n\nFunding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Schedule 4\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(a) was made:\n\n(i) under subsection 152AL(3) of the Competition and\nConsumer Act 2010; and\n\n(ii) in compliance with repealed subsection 152AL(3C) of\nthe Competition and Consumer Act 2010; and\n\n(b) was in force immediately before the commencement of\nSchedule 1 to the Telecommunications Legislation\nAmendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) during a period comprising the whole or a part of a month in\nan eligible financial year, a person is a carrier; and\n\n(b) a declaration made under subsection 63(2) of the\nTelecommunications Act 1997 was in force on 30 June 2018\nin relation to the carrier licence held by the person; and\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(c) the declaration provides that the person must (upon request\nby an end-user at relevant premises) connect, or arrange for\nanother person on the person’s behalf to connect, premises\nlocated in a development area (however described) specified\nin the declaration to a telecommunications network owned by\nthe person (as specified in the declaration); and\n\n(d) the person, or another person on the person’s behalf:\n\n(i) has connected one or more premises located in the\ndevelopment area to the telecommunications network;\nand\n\n(ii) has done so before the end of 30 June 2019; and\n\n(e) one or more of the connected premises are potentially\nchargeable premises in relation to the person for that month;\neach of the potentially chargeable premises mentioned in\nparagraph (e) are recently connected greenfield premises in\nrelation to the person for that month.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) a person is a carrier; and\n\n(b) during a period comprising the whole or a part of a month in\nan eligible financial year, the person supplies an eligible local\nbitstream access service using a local access line; and\n\n(c) during a whole or a part of that period, a carriage service\nprovider supplies a designated broadband service to one or\nmore premises using the line; and\n\n(d) one or more of those premises are potentially chargeable\npremises in relation to the person for that month;\neach of the potentially chargeable premises mentioned in\nparagraph (d) are recently connected greenfield premises in\nrelation to the person for that month.\n\n(3) In this section:\neli",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-96b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-96b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-96b-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2d33a979d24a8ee89649d5f48317f091b2e768deeca5c9eb43f2f50e2bc90bd3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-96b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "96B Recently connected greenfield premises",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 171,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) during a period comprising the whole or a part of a month in\nan eligible financial year, a person is a carrier; and\n\n(b) a declaration made under subsection 63(2) of the\nTelecommunications Act 1997 was in force on 30 June 2018\nin relation to the carrier licence held by the person; and\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(c) the declaration provides that the person must (upon request\nby an end-user at relevant premises) connect, or arrange for\nanother person on the person’s behalf to connect, premises\nlocated in a development area (however described) specified\nin the declaration to a telecommunications network owned by\nthe person (as specified in the declaration); and\n\n(d) the person, or another person on the person’s behalf:\n\n(i) has connected one or more premises located in the\ndevelopment area to the telecommunications network;\nand\n\n(ii) has done so before the end of 30 June 2019; and\n\n(e) one or more of the connected premises are potentially\nchargeable premises in relation to the person for that month;\neach of the potentially chargeable premises mentioned in\nparagraph (e) are recently connected greenfield premises in\nrelation to the person for that month.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) a person is a carrier; and\n\n(b) during a period comprising the whole or a part of a month in\nan eligible financial year, the person supplies an eligible local\nbitstream access service using a local access line; and\n\n(c) during a whole or a part of that period, a carriage service\nprovider supplies a designated broadband service to one or\nmore premises using the line; and\n\n(d) one or more of those premises are potentially chargeable\npremises in relation to the person for that month;\neach of the potentially chargeable premises mentioned in\nparagraph (d) are recently connected greenfield premises in\nrelation to the person for that month.\n\n(3) In this section:\neligible local bitstream access service means a local bitstream\naccess service that is first supplied at a time during the period:\n\n(a) beginning at the start of 1 January 2011; and\n\n(b) ending at the end of 30 June 2019.\nlocal bitstream access service has the meaning given by a\ndeclaration that:\n\nFunding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Schedule 4\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(a) was made:\n\n(i) under subsection 152AL(3) of the Competition and\nConsumer Act 2010; and\n\n(ii) in compliance with repealed subsection 152AL(3C) of\nthe Competition and Consumer Act 2010; and\n\n(b) was in force immediately before the commencement of\nSchedule 1 to the Telecommunications Legislation\nAmendment (Competition and Consumer) Act 2020."
    },
