    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-98",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "98 Charge offset certificate",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-98"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.175",
      "values:originalText": "Application\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a person is an eligible funding recipient; and\n\n(b) the ACMA has made an assessment under section 102 setting\nout the charge payable by the person for a financial year (the\ncharge financial year);\nthe person may, at any time during the period:\n\n(c) beginning when the assessment was made; and\n\n(d) ending at the end of the standard due date (within the\nmeaning of section 102D) for the charge financial year;\napply to the Secretary for the issue to the person of a charge offset\ncertificate for the charge financial year.\n\n(2) An application under subsection (1) must:\n\n(a) be in writing; and\n\n(b) be in a form approved, in writing, by the Secretary; and\n\n(c) be accompanied by such information as is specified in rules\nmade under subsection (9).\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\nIssue of certificate\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) an application under subsection (1) has been made for the\nissue to a person of a charge offset certificate for the charge\nfinancial year; and\n\n(b) the person is the holder of a nominal funding entitlement\ncertificate in relation to the next financial year; and\n\n(c) rules made under subsection (9) for the purposes of this\nparagraph are in force; and\n\n(d) the conditions set out in those rules are satisfied;\nthe Secretary must:\n\n(e) issue a certificate stating that the person is entitled to a\ncharge offset for the charge financial year equal to the\namount specified in the certificate; and\n\n(f) do so by the end of 31 March next following the charge\nfinancial year.\n\n(4) The amount specified in the certificate:\n\n(a) must be the amount ascertained in accordance with rules\nmade under subsection (9); and\n\n(b) must not exceed the nominal funding entitlement of the\nperson for the next financial year; and\n\n(c) must not exceed the annual base amount of the person for the\ncharge financial year.\n\n(5) A certificate issued under subsection (3) is to be known as a\ncharge offset certificate.\nRefusal\n\n(6) If the Secretary decides to refuse to issue a charge offset certificate\nto a person, the Secretary must give written notice of the decision\nto the person.\nCopy of certificate\n\n(7) If the Secretary issues a charge offset certificate, the Secretary\nmust give a copy of the certificate to the ACMA.\n\nFunding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Schedule 4\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\nCharge offset certificate cannot be transferred\n\n(8) A charge offset certificate cannot be transferred.\nRules\n\n(9) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make rules for the\npurposes of this section.",
      "skos:definition": "Application\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a person is an eligible funding recipient; and\n\n(b) the ACMA has made an assessment under section 102 setting\nout the charge payable by the person for a financial year (the\ncharge financial year);\nthe person may, at any time during the period:\n\n(c) beginning when the assessment was made; and\n\n(d) ending at the end of the standard due date (within the\nmeaning of section 102D) for the charge financial year;\napply to the Secretary for the issue to the person of a charge offset\ncertificate for the charge financial year.\n\n(2) An application under subsection (1) must:\n\n(a) be in writing; and\n\n(b) be in a form approved, in writing, by the Secretary; and\n\n(c) be accompanied by such information as is specified in rules\nmade under subsection (9).\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\nIssue of certificate\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) an application under subsection (1) has been made for the\nissue to a person of a charge offset certificate for the charge\nfinancial year; and\n\n(b) the person is the holder of a nominal funding entitlement\ncertificate in relation to the next financial year; and\n\n(c) rules made under subsection (9) for the purposes of this\nparagraph are in force; and\n\n(d) the conditions set out in those rules are satisfied;\nthe Secretary must:\n\n(e) issue a certificate stating that the person is entitled to a\ncharge offset for the charge financial year equal to the\namount specified in the certificate; and\n\n(f) do so by the end of 31 March next following the charge\nfinancial year.\n\n(4) The amount specified in the certificate:\n\n(a) must be the amount ascertained in accordance with rules\nmade under subsection (9); and\n\n(b) must not exceed the nominal funding entitlement of the\nperson for the next financial year; and\n\n(c) must not exceed the annual base amount of the person for the\ncharge financial year.\n\n(5) A certificate issued under",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-98-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-98-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-98-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-98-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-98-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-98-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-98-ss-7"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-98-ss-8"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-98-ss-9"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e7ad522ea327e5ba95534ef8355038ef7f7b86328c7cf9175886f60464c40d28"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-98",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "98 Charge offset certificate",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 175,
      "values:originalText": "Application\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a person is an eligible funding recipient; and\n\n(b) the ACMA has made an assessment under section 102 setting\nout the charge payable by the person for a financial year (the\ncharge financial year);\nthe person may, at any time during the period:\n\n(c) beginning when the assessment was made; and\n\n(d) ending at the end of the standard due date (within the\nmeaning of section 102D) for the charge financial year;\napply to the Secretary for the issue to the person of a charge offset\ncertificate for the charge financial year.\n\n(2) An application under subsection (1) must:\n\n(a) be in writing; and\n\n(b) be in a form approved, in writing, by the Secretary; and\n\n(c) be accompanied by such information as is specified in rules\nmade under subsection (9).\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\nIssue of certificate\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) an application under subsection (1) has been made for the\nissue to a person of a charge offset certificate for the charge\nfinancial year; and\n\n(b) the person is the holder of a nominal funding entitlement\ncertificate in relation to the next financial year; and\n\n(c) rules made under subsection (9) for the purposes of this\nparagraph are in force; and\n\n(d) the conditions set out in those rules are satisfied;\nthe Secretary must:\n\n(e) issue a certificate stating that the person is entitled to a\ncharge offset for the charge financial year equal to the\namount specified in the certificate; and\n\n(f) do so by the end of 31 March next following the charge\nfinancial year.\n\n(4) The amount specified in the certificate:\n\n(a) must be the amount ascertained in accordance with rules\nmade under subsection (9); and\n\n(b) must not exceed the nominal funding entitlement of the\nperson for the next financial year; and\n\n(c) must not exceed the annual base amount of the person for the\ncharge financial year.\n\n(5) A certificate issued under subsection (3) is to be known as a\ncharge offset certificate.\nRefusal\n\n(6) If the Secretary decides to refuse to issue a charge offset certificate\nto a person, the Secretary must give written notice of the decision\nto the person.\nCopy of certificate\n\n(7) If the Secretary issues a charge offset certificate, the Secretary\nmust give a copy of the certificate to the ACMA.\n\nFunding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Schedule 4\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\nCharge offset certificate cannot be transferred\n\n(8) A charge offset certificate cannot be transferred.\nRules\n\n(9) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make rules for the\npurposes of this section."
    },
