    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-99",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "99 Remission or refund of charge",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-99"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.177",
      "values:originalText": "Remission\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a person becomes the holder of a charge offset certificate for\na financial year; and\n\n(b) a base instalment of charge is payable by the person in\nrelation to the financial year; and\n\n(c) the base instalment of charge has not been paid;\nthe Secretary must, on behalf of the Commonwealth, remit so\nmuch of the base instalment of charge as equals the amount\nspecified in the certificate.\nNote:\nFor base instalment of charge, see section 102D.\n\n(2) The Secretary must inform the ACMA of a remission of charge\nunder subsection (1).\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) the ACMA has made an assessment under section 102 setting\nout the charge payable by a person for a financial year; and\n\n(b) the base instalment of charge is remitted, to any extent, under\nsubsection (1) of this section; and\n\n(c) the ACMA is informed of the remission;\nthe ACMA must, under subsection 102B(1), vary the assessment to\nreflect the remission.\nRefund\n\n(4) If:\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(a) a person becomes the holder of a charge offset certificate for\na financial year; and\n\n(b) a base instalment of charge was payable by the person in\nrelation to the financial year; and\n\n(c) the base instalment of charge has been paid;\nthe Secretary must, on behalf of the Commonwealth, refund so\nmuch of the base instalment of charge as equals the amount\nspecified in the certificate.\nNote:\nFor base instalment of charge, see section 102D.",
      "skos:definition": "Remission\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a person becomes the holder of a charge offset certificate for\na financial year; and\n\n(b) a base instalment of charge is payable by the person in\nrelation to the financial year; and\n\n(c) the base instalment of charge has not been paid;\nthe Secretary must, on behalf of the Commonwealth, remit so\nmuch of the base instalment of charge as equals the amount\nspecified in the certificate.\nNote:\nFor base instalment of charge, see section 102D.\n\n(2) The Secretary must inform the ACMA of a remission of charge\nunder subsection (1).\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) the ACMA has made an assessment under section 102 setting\nout the charge payable by a person for a financial year; and\n\n(b) the base instalment of charge is remitted, to any extent, under\nsubsection (1) of this section; and\n\n(c) the ACMA is informed of the remission;\nthe ACMA must, under subsection 102B(1), vary the assessment to\nreflect the remission.\nRefund\n\n(4) If:\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(a) a person becomes the holder of a charge offset certificate for\na financial year; and\n\n(b) a base instalment of charge was payable by the person in\nrelation to the financial year; and\n\n(c) the base instalment of charge has been paid;\nthe Secretary must, on behalf of the Commonwealth, refund so\nmuch of the base instalment of charge as equals the amount\nspecified in the certificate.\nNote:\nFor base instalment of charge, see section 102D.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-99-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-99-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-99-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-99-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "13d493e3219ca27150a7aa4096c4746b31725c5bacd3f994115cc0898e6674fc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-99",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "99 Remission or refund of charge",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 177,
      "values:originalText": "Remission\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a person becomes the holder of a charge offset certificate for\na financial year; and\n\n(b) a base instalment of charge is payable by the person in\nrelation to the financial year; and\n\n(c) the base instalment of charge has not been paid;\nthe Secretary must, on behalf of the Commonwealth, remit so\nmuch of the base instalment of charge as equals the amount\nspecified in the certificate.\nNote:\nFor base instalment of charge, see section 102D.\n\n(2) The Secretary must inform the ACMA of a remission of charge\nunder subsection (1).\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) the ACMA has made an assessment under section 102 setting\nout the charge payable by a person for a financial year; and\n\n(b) the base instalment of charge is remitted, to any extent, under\nsubsection (1) of this section; and\n\n(c) the ACMA is informed of the remission;\nthe ACMA must, under subsection 102B(1), vary the assessment to\nreflect the remission.\nRefund\n\n(4) If:\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(a) a person becomes the holder of a charge offset certificate for\na financial year; and\n\n(b) a base instalment of charge was payable by the person in\nrelation to the financial year; and\n\n(c) the base instalment of charge has been paid;\nthe Secretary must, on behalf of the Commonwealth, refund so\nmuch of the base instalment of charge as equals the amount\nspecified in the certificate.\nNote:\nFor base instalment of charge, see section 102D."
    },
