    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-99-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "99(4) Remission or refund of charge",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-99-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.177",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If:\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(a) a person becomes the holder of a charge offset certificate for\na financial year; and\n\n(b) a base instalment of charge was payable by the person in\nrelation to the financial year; and\n\n(c) the base instalment of charge has been paid;\nthe Secretary must, on behalf of the Commonwealth, refund so\nmuch of the base instalment of charge as equals the amount\nspecified in the certificate.\nNote:\nFor base instalment of charge, see section 102D.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If:\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(a) a person becomes the holder of a charge offset certificate for\na financial year; and\n\n(b) a base instalment of charge was payable by the person in\nrelation to the financial year; and\n\n(c) the base instalment of charge has been paid;\nthe Secretary must, on behalf of the Commonwealth, refund so\nmuch of the base instalment of charge as equals the amount\nspecified in the certificate.\nNote:\nFor base instalment of charge, see section 102D.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-99"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-99-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-99-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c7326af19dae17a5d5d6a630973fd19e175bb8e968e8e7c59fd9ccd457520e75",
      "skos:note": "Secretary must refund base instalment of charge if conditions are met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-99-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "99(4) Remission or refund of charge",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 177,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If:\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(a) a person becomes the holder of a charge offset certificate for\na financial year; and\n\n(b) a base instalment of charge was payable by the person in\nrelation to the financial year; and\n\n(c) the base instalment of charge has been paid;\nthe Secretary must, on behalf of the Commonwealth, refund so\nmuch of the base instalment of charge as equals the amount\nspecified in the certificate.\nNote:\nFor base instalment of charge, see section 102D."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-99-ss-4-norm",
