    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102c-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "102C(5) ACMA may accept statements",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-102c-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.184",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If a person is an eligible funding recipient, charge payable by the\nperson in relation to a financial year is payable in 2 instalments, as\nfollows:\n\n(a) an instalment (the base instalment) of so much of the amount\nof the charge as equals the annual base amount of the person\nfor the financial year;\n\n(b) an instalment (the administrative cost instalment) of so\nmuch of the amount of the charge as equals the annual\nadministrative cost amount of the person for the financial\nyear.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If a person is an eligible funding recipient, charge payable by the\nperson in relation to a financial year is payable in 2 instalments, as\nfollows:\n\n(a) an instalment (the base instalment) of so much of the amount\nof the charge as equals the annual base amount of the person\nfor the financial year;\n\n(b) an instalment (the administrative cost instalment) of so\nmuch of the amount of the charge as equals the annual\nadministrative cost amount of the person for the financial\nyear.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102c"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102c-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102c-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "72896ad8c4de52704f9cc58822456cc2c4c2d080c7c82a19206eff0e0074982c",
      "skos:note": "Charge payable by a person in relation to a financial year must be paid in two instalments."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-102c-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "102C(5) ACMA may accept statements",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 184,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If a person is an eligible funding recipient, charge payable by the\nperson in relation to a financial year is payable in 2 instalments, as\nfollows:\n\n(a) an instalment (the base instalment) of so much of the amount\nof the charge as equals the annual base amount of the person\nfor the financial year;\n\n(b) an instalment (the administrative cost instalment) of so\nmuch of the amount of the charge as equals the annual\nadministrative cost amount of the person for the financial\nyear."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102c-ss-5-norm",
