    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102c-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "102C(6) ACMA may accept statements",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-102c-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.184",
      "values:originalText": "(6) If a person is an eligible funding recipient, the base instalment of\ncharge payable by the person in relation to a financial year\nbecomes due and payable on:\n\n(a) if the person has made an application under subsection 98(1)\nfor a charge offset certificate for the financial year—30 April\nnext following the financial year; or\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) the standard due date for the financial year; or\n\n(ii) if the ACMA, by written notice given to the person,\nallows a later day—that later day.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) If a person is an eligible funding recipient, the base instalment of\ncharge payable by the person in relation to a financial year\nbecomes due and payable on:\n\n(a) if the person has made an application under subsection 98(1)\nfor a charge offset certificate for the financial year—30 April\nnext following the financial year; or\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) the standard due date for the financial year; or\n\n(ii) if the ACMA, by written notice given to the person,\nallows a later day—that later day.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102c"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102c-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102c-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bb0080b7daef4a7232da737f6bf87bddbe1ac17a54f1c0ccc0306e09a1df80e7",
      "skos:note": "Base instalment due on specified date"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-102c-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "102C(6) ACMA may accept statements",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 184,
      "values:originalText": "(6) If a person is an eligible funding recipient, the base instalment of\ncharge payable by the person in relation to a financial year\nbecomes due and payable on:\n\n(a) if the person has made an application under subsection 98(1)\nfor a charge offset certificate for the financial year—30 April\nnext following the financial year; or\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) the standard due date for the financial year; or\n\n(ii) if the ACMA, by written notice given to the person,\nallows a later day—that later day."
    },
