    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102p",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "102P Access to information or documents held by a carrier or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-102p"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.189",
      "values:originalText": "carriage service provider\nScope\n\n(1) This section applies to a carrier or carriage service provider if the\nACMA believes on reasonable grounds that the carrier or carriage\nservice provider has information or a document that is relevant to\nthe operation of:\n\n(a) Division 4, 5, 6 or 7 of this Part; or\n\n(b) subsection 102ZFA(4); or\n\n(c) the Telecommunications (Regional Broadband Scheme)\nCharge Act 2020.\nRequirement\n\n(2) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the carrier or carriage\nservice provider, require the carrier or carriage service provider:\n\n(a) to give to the ACMA, within the period and in the manner\nand form specified in the notice, any such information; or\n\n(b) to produce to the ACMA, within the period and in the\nmanner specified in the notice, any such documents; or\n\n(c) to make copies of any such documents and to produce to the\nACMA, within the period and in the manner specified in the\nnotice, those copies.\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(3) A period specified under subsection (2) must not be shorter than 14\ndays after the notice is given.\nCompliance\n\n(4) A carrier or carriage service provider must comply with a\nrequirement under subsection (2) to the extent that the carrier or\ncarriage service provider is capable of doing so.\n\n(5) A carrier or carriage service provider commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the ACMA has given a notice to the carrier or carriage\nservice provider under subsection (2); and\n\n(b) the carrier or carriage service provider engages in conduct;\nand\n\n(c) the carrier’s conduct, or the carriage service provider’s\nconduct, contravenes a requirement in the notice.\nPenalty for contravention of this subsection: 50 penalty units.",
      "skos:definition": "carriage service provider\nScope\n\n(1) This section applies to a carrier or carriage service provider if the\nACMA believes on reasonable grounds that the carrier or carriage\nservice provider has information or a document that is relevant to\nthe operation of:\n\n(a) Division 4, 5, 6 or 7 of this Part; or\n\n(b) subsection 102ZFA(4); or\n\n(c) the Telecommunications (Regional Broadband Scheme)\nCharge Act 2020.\nRequirement\n\n(2) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the carrier or carriage\nservice provider, require the carrier or carriage service provider:\n\n(a) to give to the ACMA, within the period and in the manner\nand form specified in the notice, any such information; or\n\n(b) to produce to the ACMA, within the period and in the\nmanner specified in the notice, any such documents; or\n\n(c) to make copies of any such documents and to produce to the\nACMA, within the period and in the manner specified in the\nnotice, those copies.\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(3) A period specified under subsection (2) must not be shorter than 14\ndays after the notice is given.\nCompliance\n\n(4) A carrier or carriage service provider must comply with a\nrequirement under subsection (2) to the extent that the carrier or\ncarriage service provider is capable of doing so.\n\n(5) A carrier or carriage service provider commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the ACMA has given a notice to the carrier or carriage\nservice provider under subsection (2); and\n\n(b) the carrier or carriage service provider engages in conduct;\nand\n\n(c) the carrier’s conduct, or the carriage service provider’s\nconduct, contravenes a requirement in the notice.\nPenalty for contravention of this subsection: 50 penalty units.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102p-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102p-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102p-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102p-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102p-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0bb6a462dc59a19a67dbaa24731d8992739e39ccf1cd9b77f35ade9181fe4345"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-102p",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "102P Access to information or documents held by a carrier or",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 189,
      "values:originalText": "carriage service provider\nScope\n\n(1) This section applies to a carrier or carriage service provider if the\nACMA believes on reasonable grounds that the carrier or carriage\nservice provider has information or a document that is relevant to\nthe operation of:\n\n(a) Division 4, 5, 6 or 7 of this Part; or\n\n(b) subsection 102ZFA(4); or\n\n(c) the Telecommunications (Regional Broadband Scheme)\nCharge Act 2020.\nRequirement\n\n(2) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the carrier or carriage\nservice provider, require the carrier or carriage service provider:\n\n(a) to give to the ACMA, within the period and in the manner\nand form specified in the notice, any such information; or\n\n(b) to produce to the ACMA, within the period and in the\nmanner specified in the notice, any such documents; or\n\n(c) to make copies of any such documents and to produce to the\nACMA, within the period and in the manner specified in the\nnotice, those copies.\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(3) A period specified under subsection (2) must not be shorter than 14\ndays after the notice is given.\nCompliance\n\n(4) A carrier or carriage service provider must comply with a\nrequirement under subsection (2) to the extent that the carrier or\ncarriage service provider is capable of doing so.\n\n(5) A carrier or carriage service provider commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the ACMA has given a notice to the carrier or carriage\nservice provider under subsection (2); and\n\n(b) the carrier or carriage service provider engages in conduct;\nand\n\n(c) the carrier’s conduct, or the carriage service provider’s\nconduct, contravenes a requirement in the notice.\nPenalty for contravention of this subsection: 50 penalty units."
    },
