    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102s",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "102S ACMA may retain documents",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-102s"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.190",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may take, and retain for as long as is necessary,\npossession of a document produced under subsection 102P(2).\n\nFunding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Schedule 4\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(2) The carrier or carriage service provider otherwise entitled to\npossession of the document is entitled to be supplied, as soon as\npracticable, with a copy certified by the ACMA to be a true copy.\n\n(3) The certified copy must be received in all courts and tribunals as\nevidence as if it were the original.\n\n(4) Until a certified copy is supplied, the ACMA must, at such times\nand places as the ACMA thinks appropriate, permit the carrier or\ncarriage service provider otherwise entitled to possession of the\ndocument, or a person authorised by that carrier or carriage service\nprovider, to inspect and make copies of, or take extracts from, the\ndocument.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACMA may take, and retain for as long as is necessary,\npossession of a document produced under subsection 102P(2).\n\nFunding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Schedule 4\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(2) The carrier or carriage service provider otherwise entitled to\npossession of the document is entitled to be supplied, as soon as\npracticable, with a copy certified by the ACMA to be a true copy.\n\n(3) The certified copy must be received in all courts and tribunals as\nevidence as if it were the original.\n\n(4) Until a certified copy is supplied, the ACMA must, at such times\nand places as the ACMA thinks appropriate, permit the carrier or\ncarriage service provider otherwise entitled to possession of the\ndocument, or a person authorised by that carrier or carriage service\nprovider, to inspect and make copies of, or take extracts from, the\ndocument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102s-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102s-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102s-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102s-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "77eeda6d8665ae78114b51733ba838f1a1f66ba98a675fc48d21050b49d1d1a1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-102s",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "102S ACMA may retain documents",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 190,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may take, and retain for as long as is necessary,\npossession of a document produced under subsection 102P(2).\n\nFunding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Schedule 4\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(2) The carrier or carriage service provider otherwise entitled to\npossession of the document is entitled to be supplied, as soon as\npracticable, with a copy certified by the ACMA to be a true copy.\n\n(3) The certified copy must be received in all courts and tribunals as\nevidence as if it were the original.\n\n(4) Until a certified copy is supplied, the ACMA must, at such times\nand places as the ACMA thinks appropriate, permit the carrier or\ncarriage service provider otherwise entitled to possession of the\ndocument, or a person authorised by that carrier or carriage service\nprovider, to inspect and make copies of, or take extracts from, the\ndocument."
    },
