        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102s-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e0d562d59cc1a9cd37fa0c2f063993ef974112c3cfd90a84e09a6589e6555f2a",
      "skos:note": "Permit inspection and copying of documents"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-102s-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "102S(4) ACMA may retain documents",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 190,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Until a certified copy is supplied, the ACMA must, at such times\nand places as the ACMA thinks appropriate, permit the carrier or\ncarriage service provider otherwise entitled to possession of the\ndocument, or a person authorised by that carrier or carriage service\nprovider, to inspect and make copies of, or take extracts from, the\ndocument."
    },
