    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102u",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "102U Access to information or documents held by an eligible",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-102u"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.191",
      "values:originalText": "funding recipient\nScope\n\n(1) This section applies to an eligible funding recipient if the ACCC\nbelieves on reasonable grounds that the eligible funding recipient\nhas information or a document that is relevant to the performance\nof any of the ACCC’s functions, or the exercise of any of the\nACCC’s powers, under the Telecommunications (Regional\nBroadband Scheme) Charge Act 2020.\nRequirement\n\n(2) The ACCC may, by written notice given to the eligible funding\nrecipient, require the eligible funding recipient:\n\n(a) to give to the ACCC, within the period and in the manner and\nform specified in the notice, any such information; or\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(b) to produce to the ACCC, within the period and in the manner\nspecified in the notice, any such documents; or\n\n(c) to make copies of any such documents and to produce to the\nACCC, within the period and in the manner specified in the\nnotice, those copies.\n\n(3) A period specified under subsection (2) must not be shorter than 14\ndays after the notice is given.\nCompliance\n\n(4) An eligible funding recipient must comply with a requirement\nunder subsection (2) to the extent that the eligible funding recipient\nis capable of doing so.\n\n(5) An eligible funding recipient commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the ACCC has given a notice to the eligible funding recipient\nunder subsection (2); and\n\n(b) the eligible funding recipient engages in conduct; and\n\n(c) the eligible funding recipient’s conduct contravenes a\nrequirement in the notice.\nPenalty for contravention of this subsection: 50 penalty units.",
      "skos:definition": "funding recipient\nScope\n\n(1) This section applies to an eligible funding recipient if the ACCC\nbelieves on reasonable grounds that the eligible funding recipient\nhas information or a document that is relevant to the performance\nof any of the ACCC’s functions, or the exercise of any of the\nACCC’s powers, under the Telecommunications (Regional\nBroadband Scheme) Charge Act 2020.\nRequirement\n\n(2) The ACCC may, by written notice given to the eligible funding\nrecipient, require the eligible funding recipient:\n\n(a) to give to the ACCC, within the period and in the manner and\nform specified in the notice, any such information; or\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(b) to produce to the ACCC, within the period and in the manner\nspecified in the notice, any such documents; or\n\n(c) to make copies of any such documents and to produce to the\nACCC, within the period and in the manner specified in the\nnotice, those copies.\n\n(3) A period specified under subsection (2) must not be shorter than 14\ndays after the notice is given.\nCompliance\n\n(4) An eligible funding recipient must comply with a requirement\nunder subsection (2) to the extent that the eligible funding recipient\nis capable of doing so.\n\n(5) An eligible funding recipient commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the ACCC has given a notice to the eligible funding recipient\nunder subsection (2); and\n\n(b) the eligible funding recipient engages in conduct; and\n\n(c) the eligible funding recipient’s conduct contravenes a\nrequirement in the notice.\nPenalty for contravention of this subsection: 50 penalty units.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102u-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102u-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102u-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102u-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102u-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "69f6a3450c18f12c7153a197d39708aa9d02d1489e4d95ac038bd4bcee04b49c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-102u",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "102U Access to information or documents held by an eligible",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 191,
      "values:originalText": "funding recipient\nScope\n\n(1) This section applies to an eligible funding recipient if the ACCC\nbelieves on reasonable grounds that the eligible funding recipient\nhas information or a document that is relevant to the performance\nof any of the ACCC’s functions, or the exercise of any of the\nACCC’s powers, under the Telecommunications (Regional\nBroadband Scheme) Charge Act 2020.\nRequirement\n\n(2) The ACCC may, by written notice given to the eligible funding\nrecipient, require the eligible funding recipient:\n\n(a) to give to the ACCC, within the period and in the manner and\nform specified in the notice, any such information; or\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(b) to produce to the ACCC, within the period and in the manner\nspecified in the notice, any such documents; or\n\n(c) to make copies of any such documents and to produce to the\nACCC, within the period and in the manner specified in the\nnotice, those copies.\n\n(3) A period specified under subsection (2) must not be shorter than 14\ndays after the notice is given.\nCompliance\n\n(4) An eligible funding recipient must comply with a requirement\nunder subsection (2) to the extent that the eligible funding recipient\nis capable of doing so.\n\n(5) An eligible funding recipient commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the ACCC has given a notice to the eligible funding recipient\nunder subsection (2); and\n\n(b) the eligible funding recipient engages in conduct; and\n\n(c) the eligible funding recipient’s conduct contravenes a\nrequirement in the notice.\nPenalty for contravention of this subsection: 50 penalty units."
    },
