    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102za",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "102ZA Disclosure of information by the ACCC to certain bodies",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-102za"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.194",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACCC may disclose information to any of the following\nbodies:\n\n(a) the Department;\n\n(b) the ACMA;\n\n(c) the Regional Telecommunications Independent Review\nCommittee;\n\n(d) the Department administered by the Minister administering\nthe Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act\n2013;\n\n(e) the Department administered by the Treasurer;\n\n(f) an authorised government agency (see subsection (2));\nif:\n\n(g) the information was obtained under, or for the purposes of,\nthis Division or section 102ZF; and\n\n(h) the ACCC is satisfied that the information will enable or\nassist the body to perform or exercise any of the functions or\npowers of the body.\n\nFunding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Schedule 4\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(2) The ACCC may, by notifiable instrument, declare that a specified\ndepartment or authority of the Commonwealth, a State or a\nTerritory is an authorised government agency for the purposes of\nparagraph (1)(f).\n\n(3) The ACCC may, by writing, impose conditions to be complied\nwith in relation to information disclosed under subsection (1).\n\n(4) An instrument made under subsection (3) that imposes conditions\nrelating to one particular disclosure identified in the instrument is a\nnotifiable instrument.\n\n(5) Otherwise, an instrument made under subsection (3) is a legislative\ninstrument.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACCC may disclose information to any of the following\nbodies:\n\n(a) the Department;\n\n(b) the ACMA;\n\n(c) the Regional Telecommunications Independent Review\nCommittee;\n\n(d) the Department administered by the Minister administering\nthe Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act\n2013;\n\n(e) the Department administered by the Treasurer;\n\n(f) an authorised government agency (see subsection (2));\nif:\n\n(g) the information was obtained under, or for the purposes of,\nthis Division or section 102ZF; and\n\n(h) the ACCC is satisfied that the information will enable or\nassist the body to perform or exercise any of the functions or\npowers of the body.\n\nFunding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband  Schedule 4\n\nNo. 47, 2020\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\n\n(2) The ACCC may, by notifiable instrument, declare that a specified\ndepartment or authority of the Commonwealth, a State or a\nTerritory is an authorised government agency for the purposes of\nparagraph (1)(f).\n\n(3) The ACCC may, by writing, impose conditions to be complied\nwith in relation to information disclosed under subsection (1).\n\n(4) An instrument made under subsection (3) that imposes conditions\nrelating to one particular disclosure identified in the instrument is a\nnotifiable instrument.\n\n(5) Otherwise, an instrument made under subsection (3) is a legislative\ninstrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102za-ss-1"
        },
