    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102zb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "102ZB Register of Contracts for the Funding of Fixed Wireless",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-102zb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020.pdf, p.195",
      "values:originalText": "Broadband and Satellite Broadband\n\n(1) The Secretary is to maintain a register, to be known as the Register\nof Contracts for the Funding of Fixed Wireless Broadband and\nSatellite Broadband, in which the Secretary includes the following\nfor each section 80 contract that is in force:\n\n(a) the name of the contractor;\n\n(b) the duration of the contract;\n\n(c) if the contract requires actions to be undertaken by the\ncontractor—a summary of those actions;\n\n(d) if the contract requires services, facilities or customer\nequipment to be supplied by the contractor—a description of\nthose services, facilities or customer equipment;\n\n(e) if the contract provides for the Commonwealth to reimburse,\nor partly reimburse, costs or expenses—a description of those\ncosts or expenses;\n\n(f) one of the following:\n\n(i) the total amount paid or to be paid by the\nCommonwealth under the contract;\n\n(ii) an estimate of the total amount paid or to be paid by the\nCommonwealth under the contract;\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(iii) the method of working out the total amount paid or to\nbe paid by the Commonwealth under the contract.\n\n(2) The Register of Contracts for the Funding of Fixed Wireless\nBroadband and Satellite Broadband is to be maintained by\nelectronic means.\n\n(3) The Register of Contracts for the Funding of Fixed Wireless\nBroadband and Satellite Broadband is to be made available for\ninspection on the Department’s website.\n\n(4) The Register of Contracts for the Funding of Fixed Wireless\nBroadband and Satellite Broadband is not a legislative instrument.",
      "skos:definition": "Broadband and Satellite Broadband\n\n(1) The Secretary is to maintain a register, to be known as the Register\nof Contracts for the Funding of Fixed Wireless Broadband and\nSatellite Broadband, in which the Secretary includes the following\nfor each section 80 contract that is in force:\n\n(a) the name of the contractor;\n\n(b) the duration of the contract;\n\n(c) if the contract requires actions to be undertaken by the\ncontractor—a summary of those actions;\n\n(d) if the contract requires services, facilities or customer\nequipment to be supplied by the contractor—a description of\nthose services, facilities or customer equipment;\n\n(e) if the contract provides for the Commonwealth to reimburse,\nor partly reimburse, costs or expenses—a description of those\ncosts or expenses;\n\n(f) one of the following:\n\n(i) the total amount paid or to be paid by the\nCommonwealth under the contract;\n\n(ii) an estimate of the total amount paid or to be paid by the\nCommonwealth under the contract;\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(iii) the method of working out the total amount paid or to\nbe paid by the Commonwealth under the contract.\n\n(2) The Register of Contracts for the Funding of Fixed Wireless\nBroadband and Satellite Broadband is to be maintained by\nelectronic means.\n\n(3) The Register of Contracts for the Funding of Fixed Wireless\nBroadband and Satellite Broadband is to be made available for\ninspection on the Department’s website.\n\n(4) The Register of Contracts for the Funding of Fixed Wireless\nBroadband and Satellite Broadband is not a legislative instrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102zb-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102zb-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102zb-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020-sch-4-sec-102zb-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c083aa6c4eecd85d46eff71258d9c786e62b581ac22fa9cc894151b53185e87f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-102zb",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "102ZB Register of Contracts for the Funding of Fixed Wireless",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 195,
      "values:originalText": "Broadband and Satellite Broadband\n\n(1) The Secretary is to maintain a register, to be known as the Register\nof Contracts for the Funding of Fixed Wireless Broadband and\nSatellite Broadband, in which the Secretary includes the following\nfor each section 80 contract that is in force:\n\n(a) the name of the contractor;\n\n(b) the duration of the contract;\n\n(c) if the contract requires actions to be undertaken by the\ncontractor—a summary of those actions;\n\n(d) if the contract requires services, facilities or customer\nequipment to be supplied by the contractor—a description of\nthose services, facilities or customer equipment;\n\n(e) if the contract provides for the Commonwealth to reimburse,\nor partly reimburse, costs or expenses—a description of those\ncosts or expenses;\n\n(f) one of the following:\n\n(i) the total amount paid or to be paid by the\nCommonwealth under the contract;\n\n(ii) an estimate of the total amount paid or to be paid by the\nCommonwealth under the contract;\n\nSchedule 4  Funding of fixed wireless broadband and satellite broadband\n\nTelecommunications Legislation Amendment (Competition and\nConsumer) Act 2020\nNo. 47, 2020\n\n(iii) the method of working out the total amount paid or to\nbe paid by the Commonwealth under the contract.\n\n(2) The Register of Contracts for the Funding of Fixed Wireless\nBroadband and Satellite Broadband is to be maintained by\nelectronic means.\n\n(3) The Register of Contracts for the Funding of Fixed Wireless\nBroadband and Satellite Broadband is to be made available for\ninspection on the Department’s website.\n\n(4) The Register of Contracts for the Funding of Fixed Wireless\nBroadband and Satellite Broadband is not a legislative instrument."
    },
