      "cml:integrityHash": "4dd7ddcdb988974ea2313c487348f675eed1cf26b94ca31a0ddbeae5ffe58672",
      "skos:note": "Resolution to disallow determination within 15 sitting days Public consultation must be provided during a review under subsection (1).",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-1-3-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1(2) July 2019 instead of the designated start date); and",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 199,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Either House of the Parliament may, following a motion upon\nnotice, pass a resolution disallowing the determination. For the\nresolution to be effective:\n\n(a) the notice must be given in that House within 15 sitting days\nof that House after the copy of the determination was tabled\nin the House under section 38 of the Legislation Act 2003;\nand\n\n(b) the resolution must be passed, in pursuance of the motion,\nwithin 15 sitting days of that House after the giving of that\nnotice."
    },
