      "cml:integrityHash": "5b55277d715110ac5bef2f2348a565dcf00e89e4760a41e677b7451ac8fb21eb",
      "skos:note": "The Minister may give the ACMA a written direction requiring the ACMA to make available specified information. Section 42 of the Legislation Act 2003 does not apply to the determination. Verification of statements in the report may be required."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-legislation-amendment-competition-and-consumer-act-2020#sch-4-sec-1-3-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1(4) July 2019 instead of the designated start date); and",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 199,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Section 42 (disallowance) of the Legislation Act 2003 does not\napply to the determination.\nNote 1:\nThe 15 sitting day notice period mentioned in paragraph (2)(a) of this\nsection is the same as the 15 sitting day notice period mentioned in\nparagraph 42(1)(a) of the Legislation Act 2003.\nNote 2:\nThe 15 sitting day disallowance period mentioned in paragraph (2)(b)\nof this section is the same as the 15 sitting day disallowance period\nmentioned in paragraph 42(1)(b) of the Legislation Act 2003."
    },
